    "https://careers.rpi.edu/jobs/assistant-coach-women-s-hockey-troy-ny-new-york-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach, Women's Hockey",
      "description": "Assistant Coach, Women's Hockey - Troy, NY, New York, United States Back to RPI Website My Profile Kiosk mode Assistant Coach, Women's Hockey Troy, NY Athletics Staff Full Time Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary: The duties and responsibilities of the Assistant Coach for Women’s Ice Hockey are to assist the Head Coach in the management and administration of a Division I Women’s Hockey program. The core responsibilities of the Assistant Coach are to recommend, implement and execute a successful recruiting philosophy and strategy to ensure student-athletes are committed and engaged academically, athletically, and socially. In addition, the Assistant Coach is responsible for preparing student-athletes both on and off the ice with instruction of an academic and personal nature. The Assistant Coach will also serve as coordinator for position-specific players and will assist in the development of all position players. Who we are: Founded in 1824, Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute (RPI) is the first technological research university in the United States. We bring creativity, science, and technology together to address society's greatest challenges. We cultivate exceptional problem-solvers by immersing them in a culture of rigorous inquiry, disciplined practice, and hands-on application. Our strategic plan, RPI Forward, charts a pioneering course for the next era of RPI. Explore the RPI Forward plan. ↗︎ Nestled on a beautiful 275-acre campus in upstate NY, RPI is home to five schools, 32 research centers, three makerspaces, an observatory, one of the world’s fastest supercomputers, and the IBM Quantum System One - the first university-based quantum computer in the world. With top notch employee health and retirement benefits, Rensselaer offers its full-time employees a generous paid time off program, tuition remission, and opportunities for career growth. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in a related field. One (1) year of experience related to ice hockey, including experience supervising, communicating with, and instructing student-athletes and prospective student-athletes. Valid U.S. driver's license. Applicants must meet stated minimum education and experience requirements. Preferred Qualifications: Collegiate playing and/or coaching experience in ice hockey, including recruiting, player development, NCAA compliance, and student-athlete support. Minimum Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Knowledge of NCAA regulations and guidelines governing the recruitment and retention of student-athletes. Familiarity of athletic recruitment methods and techniques. Ability to initiate, develop and maintain appropriate contacts. Demonstrated commitment to diversity and inclusion Ability to work with a diverse population of student-athletes, parents, coaches, and administrators Strong interpersonal and communication skills Ability to read, understand, follow, and enforce safety procedures. Ability to foster a cooperative work environment. Ability to identify athletic skill levels of potential student athletes Representative Job Duties: Serve as a coordinator for position-specific players and special teams. Assess individual and team skills and abilities, on and off the ice, and develop strategies for capitalizing on strengths and improving weaknesses. Organize, prepare, and conduct individual and team practices, games, training, and competition. Create and maintain an environment that emphasizes academic progress and places the welfare, retention, eligibility, and graduation of student-athletes at the forefront of the program. Assist in administering study hall and other academic support needs of student-athletes. Coordinate the admissions process for incoming first-year students from application through admission decision in collaboration with the Admissions Office. In consultation with the Head Coach, implement and execute a successful recruiting philosophy and strategy that attracts student-athletes who will succeed both academically and athletically. Coordinate all communication with prospective student-athletes and manage official and unofficial campus visits. Ensure the Women's Hockey program complies with all NCAA, conference, and RPI rules and policies related to the recruitment, eligibility, and retention of first-year, transfer, and continuing student-athletes. Coordinate community and campus events and activities. Participate in and support fundraising, marketing, and promotional events as assigned. Work with alumni and support alumni engagement activities for the Women's Hockey program. Shift: Non Standard Shift: Non-standard work schedule, including evenings, weekends, holidays, and extended hours during the competitive season, recruiting periods, team travel, and special events. Travel: Significant travel (greater than 25%) is required for recruiting, NCAA competition, team travel, professional development, and other program-related activities. Overnight and weekend travel is expected. Driving: Must be able to operate a vehicle for business purposes, including recruiting, team travel, and attendance at university and community events. A valid driver's license and the ability to meet the Institute's driver authorization requirements are required. Starting Salary/Rate: Expected hiring range: $75,000 - $81,500 Pay transparency disclosure: The selected candidate’s salary will be determined based on factors that include the available budget, internal equity, and the final candidate’s qualifications, experience, education and other job-related credentials. This hiring range is provided as Rensselaer’s good faith estimate of the expected hiring range at the time of posting. Application instructions: Follow the on-screen prompts to create a brief online profile. Please be ready to upload your resume and cover letter. If you need assistance with the online application process, please contact careers@rpi.edu. Job Posted Date: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Total Compensation and Benefits Information: Rensselaer’s Total Compensation Program is designed to provide stable pay growth, a comprehensive and affordable benefits package, and a comprehensive and affordable retiree medical and prescription plan. Our goal is to provide you and your family with a comprehensive health and welfare program as an umbrella of financial security and protection during your employment. For more information, please visit Benefits | Human Resources (rpi.edu) . Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is committed to the cultivation of a community that is welcoming, inclusive, and above all values learning. We welcome candidates who bring a variety of perspectives to Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute's work and campus communities. Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation or gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or other characteristic protected by law. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) f84cd6fa Last Name (required) e0b13442 Email (required) 34ba9b4e Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Assistant Coach, Women's Lacrosse Troy, NY ICA Sports The Assistant Coach, Women's Lacrosse provides coaching, recruiting, and administrative support to the Head Coach in all aspects of the Women's Lacrosse program. This position assists with planning and conducting practices and competitions, instructing and mentoring student-athletes, identifying and recruiting qualified prospective student-athletes, supporting academic success, and promoting student-athlete development on and off the field. The Assistant Coach also assists with program operations, fundraising, alumni engagement, team travel, NCAA and conference compliance, and other administrative responsibilities that contribute to the success and competitiveness of the Women's Lacrosse program. Deputy Title IX Coordinator / Equal Opportunity Specialist Hybrid: in-office and remote work. Troy, NY Human Resources Office The Deputy Title IX Coordinator / Equal Opportunity Specialist supports the Institute’s commitment to an equitable, inclusive, and discrimination-free living, learning, and working environment. The position provides dedicated support for the effective administration of the Institute’s Title IX, Equal Opportunity, Title VI, and related civil rights compliance programs, helping ensure fair, thorough, and supportive processes for all participants. Space Planning Coordinator Hybrid: in-office and remote work. Troy, NY Campus Planning & Facilities Design Coordinates campus space planning, occupancy, and departmental moves while partnering with academic and administrative stakeholders to develop practical space solutions. Supports space data management, CAD-based planning, project coordination, and successful workplace transitions across the Institute. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 3fa3b232 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Athletics Staff Athletics Staff Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Troy, NY, New York, United States Troy, NY, New York, United States First Name (required) 631c3c88 Last Name (required) 4d4b26de Email (required) 024b6f9a Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026 Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute (RPI) Cookie Preferences Web Privacy TileX Student Consumer Information Accessibilityy Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your 