      "title": "Assistant Coach, Women's Lacrosse",
      "description": "Assistant Coach, Women's Lacrosse - Troy, NY, New York, United States Back to RPI Website My Profile Kiosk mode Assistant Coach, Women's Lacrosse Troy, NY Athletics Staff Full Time Closing on: Sep 17 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary: Provide coaching and administrative assistance to the Head Coach. Oversee one or more specified areas of a sporting discipline or a component of a team, and assist the Head Coach with all aspects of recruitment and training of athletes. Who we are: Founded in 1824, Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute (RPI) is the first technological research university in the United States. We bring creativity, science, and technology together to address society's greatest challenges. We cultivate exceptional problem-solvers by immersing them in a culture of rigorous inquiry, disciplined practice, and hands-on application. Our strategic plan, RPI Forward, charts a pioneering course for the next era of RPI. Explore the RPI Forward plan. ↗︎ Nestled on a beautiful 275-acre campus in upstate NY, RPI is home to five schools, 32 research centers, three makerspaces, an observatory, one of the world’s fastest supercomputers, and the IBM Quantum System One - the first university-based quantum computer in the world. With top notch employee health and retirement benefits, Rensselaer offers its full-time employees a generous paid time off program, tuition remission, and opportunities for career growth. Minimum Qualifications: Minimum Education: Bachelor's degree or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Minimum Experience: One (1) year experience specific to Lacrosse. Relevant combinations of education, training and experience may be considered. Preferred Qualifications: Valid driver's license preferred for occasional recruiting, team travel, and other Athletics-related responsibilities. Minimum Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Knowledge and understanding of all aspects of the specified sports program. Knowledge of NCAA regulations and guidelines governing the recruitment and retention of student-athletes. Familiarity of athletic recruitment methods and techniques. Ability to guide student-athletes in area of specialty. Ability to initiate, develop and maintain appropriate contacts. Strong interpersonal and communication skills Ability to communicate effectively, both orally and in writing. Ability to read, understand, follow, and enforce safety procedures. Ability to foster a cooperative work environment. Ability to identify athletic skill levels of potential student athletes Representative Job Duties: Participate in the creation of a successful team by carrying out duties assigned by the Head Coach, including: Organize, prepare, and conduct individual and team practices, training, and competition. Coordinate one or more specified areas of a sporting discipline and/or a component of a team. Assess individual abilities during practices and competitions, and devise strategies for capitalizing on strengths and improving weaknesses. As directed by the Head Coach, support the academic success of student-athletes through such activities as running study halls, maintaining grade books, enforcing class attendance, and directing students to the appropriate resources. Provide an example of and advise students on life skills such as teamwork, cooperation, time management, handling adversity, failure, and success. Increase the knowledge and skill level of student-athletes in their sport. In consultation with the Head Coach, organize and execute a successful recruiting program through cooperative efforts with the Office of Admissions and the Department of Athletics. Organize fundraising events such as alumni golf outings or tournaments as assigned. Provide administrative support for other fundraising events, such as mail campaigns. Participate in off-season events such as camps, community coaching, and other activities to promote fundraising and recruiting. Participate in other fundraising, marketing, or promotional activities as assigned. Carry out tasks as assigned to assist the Head Coach in the management of the people, facilities, and other resources needed to effectively operate the team. This includes, but is not limited to: Plan for team travel. Prepare and submit purchasing and travel requests. Schedule games, meets, and matches. Manage games, meets, and matches when hosting home contests. Ensure NCAA and conference rule compliance. Shift: Primarily business hours. Regular evening and weekend hours are required during the competitive season to support practices, competitions, recruiting activities, team travel, and other Athletics events. Travel: Occasional overnight travel (10% or less) may be required for team competition, recruiting, conferences, professional development, and other Athletics-related activities. Driving: Incidental driving may occur for recruiting, team travel, or other Athletics-related activities; however, driving is not an essential function of the position. Starting Salary/Rate: Expected hiring range: $16.25 This is a full-time, 10-month appointment. Housing benefit eligible. Additional Benefit:  Institute-owned housing may be available for this position based on operational needs and institutional approval. Depending on the circumstances, the value of the housing may be treated as taxable income in accordance with IRS requirements. This position is appointed on a 10-month work schedule and includes scheduled furlough periods. Employees are expected to return to active employment following each furlough period. Institute-owned housing may continue to be provided during furlough periods for returning employees, subject to operational needs, institutional approval, and applicable IRS tax requirements. Pay transparency disclosure: The selected candidate’s salary will be determined based on factors that include the available budget, internal equity, and the final candidate’s qualifications, experience, education and other job-related credentials. This hiring range is provided as Rensselaer’s good faith estimate of the expected hiring range at the time of posting. Application instructions: Follow the on-screen prompts to create a brief online profile. Please be ready to upload your resume and cover letter. If you need assistance with the online application process, please contact careers@rpi.edu. Job Posted Date: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Total Compensation and Benefits Information: Rensselaer’s Total Compensation Program is designed to provide stable pay growth, a comprehensive and affordable benefits package, and a comprehensive and affordable retiree medical and prescription plan. Our goal is to provide you and your family with a comprehensive health and welfare program as an umbrella of financial security and protection during your employment. For more information, please visit Benefits | Human Resources (rpi.edu) . Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is committed to the cultivation of a community that is welcoming, inclusive, and above all values learning. We welcome candidates who bring a variety of perspectives to Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute's work and campus communities. Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation or gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or other characteristic protected by law. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) bf14e6f9 Last Name (required) f5c54428 Email (required) f0d3899e Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Assistant Coach, Women's Hockey Troy, NY Athletics The duties and responsibilities of the Assistant Coach for Women’s Ice Hockey are to assist the Head Coach in the management and administration of a Division I Women’s Hockey program. The core responsibilities of the Assistant Coach are to recommend, implement and execute a successful recruiting philosophy and strategy to ensure student-athletes are committed and engaged academically, athletically, and socially. In addition, the Assistant Coach is responsible for preparing student-athletes both on and off the ice with instruction of an academic and personal nature. The Assistant Coach will also serve as coordinator for position-specific players and will assist in the development of all position players. Deputy Title IX Coordinator / Equal Opportunity Specialist Hybrid: in-office and remote work. Troy, NY Human Resources Office The Deputy Title IX Coordinator / Equal Opportunity Specialist supports the Institute’s commitment to an equitable, inclusive, and discrimination-free living, learning, and working environment. The position provides dedicated support for the effective administration of the Institute’s Title IX, Equal Opportunity, Title VI, and related civil rights compliance programs, helping ensure fair, thorough, and supportive processes for all participants. Space Planning Coordinator Hybrid: in-office and remote work. Troy, NY Campus Planning & Facilities Design Coordinates campus space planning, occupancy, and departmental moves while partnering with academic and administrative stakeholders to develop practical space solutions. Supports space data management, CAD-based planning, project coordination, and successful workplace transitions across the Institute. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert c6f2c00d Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Athletics Staff Athletics Staff Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Troy, NY, New York, United States Troy, NY, New York, United States First Name (required) 463e947f Last Name (required) dba9d5e2 Email (requi