    "https://careers.rpi.edu/jobs/deputy-title-ix-coordinator-equal-opportunity-specialist-troy-ny-new-york-united-states-hybrid-in-office-and-remote-work": {
      "title": "Deputy Title IX Coordinator / Equal Opportunity Specialist",
      "description": "Deputy Title IX Coordinator / Equal Opportunity Specialist - Troy, NY, New York, United States - Hybrid: in-office and remote work, New York, United States Back to RPI Website My Profile Kiosk mode Deputy Title IX Coordinator / Equal Opportunity Specialist Hybrid: in-office and remote work Troy, NY CFHE Human Resources Staff Full Time Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary: The Deputy Title IX Coordinator / Equal Opportunity Specialist supports the Institute’s commitment to an equitable, inclusive, and discrimination-free living, learning, and working environment. The position provides dedicated support for the effective administration of the Institute’s Title IX, Equal Opportunity, Title VI, and related civil rights compliance programs, helping ensure fair, thorough, and supportive processes for all participants. Who we are: Founded in 1824, Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute (RPI) is the first technological research university in the United States. We bring creativity, science, and technology together to address society's greatest challenges. We cultivate exceptional problem-solvers by immersing them in a culture of rigorous inquiry, disciplined practice, and hands-on application. Our strategic plan, RPI Forward, charts a pioneering course for the next era of RPI. Explore the RPI Forward plan. ↗︎ Nestled on a beautiful 275-acre campus in upstate NY, RPI is home to five schools, 32 research centers, three makerspaces, an observatory, one of the world’s fastest supercomputers, and the IBM Quantum System One - the first university-based quantum computer in the world. With top notch employee health and retirement benefits, Rensselaer offers its full-time employees a generous paid time off program, tuition remission, and opportunities for career growth. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree. Five (5) or more years of progressively responsible experience in Title IX, employee relations, civil rights or equal opportunity compliance, investigations, human resources, higher education administration, student affairs, or a related field, including substantial experience in the practical application of federal and state equal opportunity and civil rights laws. Experience administering Title IX or comparable civil rights investigation, resolution, and compliance processes. Experience analyzing complex factual situations and developing, interpreting, and applying complex policies and procedures. Title IX compliance training or certification, or the ability to complete appropriate training within sixty (60) days of employment. Relevant combinations of education, training and experience may be considered. Preferred Qualifications: Master's Degree. Higher education experience. Experience conducting Title IX, Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO), workplace, student conduct, or civil rights investigations. Certification or specialized training in Title IX compliance or investigation procedures. SUNY Student Conduct Institute, NACUA, ATIXA, or other industry-related certifications are preferred. Minimum Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Knowledge of and demonstrated ability to interpret federal and state harassment and non-discrimination laws and regulations, including Title VI, Title VII, Title IX, and other applicable federal, state and local laws and regulations. Ability to prioritize and coordinate multiple complex projects simultaneously while adhering to strict deadlines. Strong presentation and facilitation skills with emphasis on education and training. Effective written and verbal communication skills. Exceptional attention to detail and accuracy of work. Ability to exercise sound judgment and maintain the highest level of confidentiality. Ability to navigate sensitive and difficult situations with professionalism, discretion, and respect for all participants. Ability to both work independently and establish effective working relationships with internal and external partners. Ability to work with sensitive information in a high volume, fast-paced environment with changing priorities and meet established goals and objectives. Demonstrated proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite. Representative Job Duties: Serve as Deputy Title IX Coordinator, coordinating and administering Title IX processes in a fair, consistent, and unbiased manner, including delegated responsibilities related to intake, supportive measures, notices, case management, informal and formal resolution processes, and other program requirements. - Receive reports and complaints involving discrimination, harassment, sexual misconduct, and retaliation; conduct intake and initial assessment; and coordinate appropriate response, supportive measures, referrals, notifications, and resolution processes in a manner that promotes fairness and respect for the rights of all parties. Conduct thorough, impartial investigations involving alleged discrimination, harassment, retaliation, and other civil rights or Institute policy violations, as assigned. Maintain accurate and complete confidential case files, records, databases, and compliance documentation. Develop and deliver training, education, prevention, and outreach programs related to Title IX, Equal Opportunity, discrimination, harassment, and respectful workplace practices for students, faculty, and staff. Support Equal Opportunity initiatives, including employment data analysis and identification of potential barriers to equal opportunity in recruitment, hiring, and advancement. Monitor changes in applicable laws and regulations and recommend appropriate updates to policies, procedures, training, and educational materials, and contribute to institutional, federal, and state data reporting and compliance reviews. - Analyze trends and data, identify emerging culture and climate concerns related to equal opportunity and civil rights, and recommend responsive interventions and improvements to Institute programs, practices, and processes. Collaborate with Student Experience, legal counsel, managers and supervisors, and other campus partners regarding policy, compliance, and appropriate response to concerns. Other duties as assigned. Shift: Business Hours: Monday - Friday Travel: Local travel between campus locations only Driving: Incidental driving possible, but not required Starting Salary/Rate: Expected hiring range: $83,600 - $100,000 Pay transparency disclosure: The selected candidate’s salary will be determined based on factors that include the available budget, internal equity, and the final candidate’s qualifications, experience, education and other job-related credentials. This hiring range is provided as Rensselaer’s good faith estimate of the expected hiring range at the time of posting. Application instructions: Follow the on-screen prompts to create a brief online profile. Please be ready to upload your resume and cover letter. If you need assistance with the online application process, please contact careers@rpi.edu. Job Posted Date: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Total Compensation and Benefits Information: Rensselaer’s Total Compensation Program is designed to provide stable pay growth, a comprehensive and affordable benefits package, and a comprehensive and affordable retiree medical and prescription plan. Our goal is to provide you and your family with a comprehensive health and welfare program as an umbrella of financial security and protection during your employment. For more information, please visit Benefits | Human Resources (rpi.edu) . Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is committed to the cultivation of a community that is welcoming, inclusive, and above all values learning. We welcome candidates who bring a variety of perspectives to Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute's work and campus communities. Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation or gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or other characteristic protected by law. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 336cde2d Last Name (required) 0d4e1a29 Email (required) 80da16b2 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Assistant Coach, Women's Hockey Troy, NY Athletics The duties and responsibilities of the Assistant Coach for Women’s Ice Hockey are to assist the Head Coach in the management and administration of a Division I Women’s Hockey program. The core responsibilities of the Assistant Coach are to recommend, implement and execute a successful recruiting philosophy and strategy to ensure student-athletes are committed and engaged academically, athletically, and socially. In addition, the Assistant Coach is responsible for preparing student-athletes both on and off the ice with instruction of an academic and personal nature. The Assistant Coach will also serve as coordinator for position-specific players and will assist in the development of all position players. Assistant Coach, Women's Lacrosse Troy, NY ICA Sports The Assistant Coach, Women's Lacrosse provides coaching, recruiting, and administrative support to the Head Coach in all aspects of the Women's Lacrosse program. This position assists with planning and conducting practices and competitions, instructing and mentoring student-athletes, identifying and recruiting qualified prospective student-athletes, supporting academic success, and promoting student-athlete development on and off the field. The Assistant Coach also assists with program operations, fundraising, alumni engagement, team travel, NCAA and conference compliance, and other administrative responsibilities that contribute to the success and competitiveness of the Women's Lacrosse program. Space Planning Coordinator Hybrid: in-office and remote work. Troy, NY Campus Planning & Facilities Design Coordinates campus space planning, occupancy, and departmental moves while partnering with academic and administrative stakeholders to develop practical space solutions. Supports space data management, CAD-based planning, project coordination, and successful workplace transitions across the Institute. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert a763d9f0 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories CFHE Human Resources Staff CFHE Human Resources Staff Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Hybrid: in-office and remote work, New York, United States Troy, NY, New York, United States Hybrid: in-office and remote work, New York, United States Troy, NY, New York, United States First Name (required) 42a3dd7b Last Name (required) 2a26c770 Email (required) e762d063 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026 Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute (RPI) Cookie Preferences Web Privacy TileX Student Consumer Information Accessibilityy Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
