    "https://careers.rpi.edu/jobs/space-planning-coordinator-troy-ny-new-york-united-states-hybrid-in-office-and-remote-work": {
      "title": "Space Planning Coordinator",
      "description": "Space Planning Coordinator - Troy, NY, New York, United States - Hybrid: in-office and remote work, New York, United States Back to RPI Website My Profile Kiosk mode Space Planning Coordinator Hybrid: in-office and remote work Troy, NY CFHE Staff Student Services and Academic Support Full Time Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary: The Space Planning Coordinator supports the effective planning, implementation, and coordination of campus space resources across RPI facilities. Working closely with academic and administrative departments, this position coordinates space requests, occupancy planning, departmental relocations, and implementation of approved space assignments. The Coordinator serves as the primary liaison for space-related changes, ensuring accurate space records, effective communication, and seamless occupancy transitions that support the Institute's strategic, academic, and operational priorities. Who we are: Founded in 1824, Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute (RPI) is the first technological research university in the United States. We bring creativity, science, and technology together to address society's greatest challenges. We cultivate exceptional problem-solvers by immersing them in a culture of rigorous inquiry, disciplined practice, and hands-on application. Our strategic plan, RPI Forward, charts a pioneering course for the next era of RPI. Explore the RPI Forward plan. ↗︎ Nestled on a beautiful 275-acre campus in upstate NY, RPI is home to five schools, 32 research centers, three makerspaces, an observatory, one of the world’s fastest supercomputers, and the IBM Quantum System One - the first university-based quantum computer in the world. With top notch employee health and retirement benefits, Rensselaer offers its full-time employees a generous paid time off program, tuition remission, and opportunities for career growth. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Facilities Management, Architecture, Interior Design, Planning, Construction Management, Business Administration, or a related field. Three (3) or more years of progressively responsible experience in space planning, facilities planning, move management, workplace planning, project coordination, or a related field. Experience coordinating projects involving multiple stakeholders. Experience coordinating space relocations and occupancy planning. Experience using CAD software and maintaining space-related information and databases. Strong communication, organizational, customer service, and project coordination skills. Relevant combinations of education, training and experience may be considered. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in higher education, healthcare, research, or another complex institutional environment. Experience supporting FICM classifications, Higher Education Facilities Inventory surveys, or institutional space reporting. Experience with FMS:Workplace or similar integrated workplace or space management systems. Familiarity with campus planning, capital projects, and institutional space governance. Minimum Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Knowledge of facilities planning, occupancy planning, and workplace planning principles. Understanding of higher education space allocation processes and institutional operations. Ability to interpret architectural drawings, floor plans, and occupancy layouts. Strong project coordination, organizational, and communication skills. Ability to build consensus among diverse stakeholders. Proficiency with AutoCAD, Microsoft Office applications, and Integrated Workplace Management Systems (IWMS) such as FMS:Workplace, Archibus, Planon, or similar software. Attention to detail and commitment to maintaining accurate records. Representative Job Duties: Space Planning & Coordination Serve as the primary point of contact for academic and administrative departments requesting space planning, occupancy changes, and relocation support. Manage the intake, tracking, routing, and communication of campus space requests through established governance processes. Partner with stakeholders to assess space needs, evaluate alternatives, and recommend practical space solutions. Develop preliminary occupancy plans and space layout options consistent with Institute standards and planning guidelines. Coordinate approved space assignments, reallocations, and occupancy changes while responding to evolving institutional priorities and operational needs. Support the implementation of Institute space standards, workplace guidelines, and space allocation practices. Move Management Plan and coordinate departmental relocations associated with renovations, capital projects, reorganizations, and other strategic initiatives. Develop move schedules, transition plans, occupancy sequencing, and communication plans to ensure successful project execution. Coordinate activities among departments, vendors, and project teams throughout the relocation process. Ensure occupancy readiness by coordinating furniture, signage, telecommunications, access control, equipment, and other move-in requirements. Monitor move activities, proactively address scheduling and logistical issues, and escalate concerns as appropriate. Conduct pre- and post-occupancy walkthroughs to verify readiness and resolve transition issues. Space Data Coordination & Governance Collaborate with the Space Information Analyst to maintain accurate campus space inventory, occupancy, utilization, and assignment records. Assist with field verification, occupancy audits, and data validation activities. Verify completed occupancy assignments and coordinate system updates following departmental moves. Support the collection and validation of institutional space data for FICM, higher education surveys, and other reporting requirements. Coordinate move requests and occupancy workflows within the Institute's integrated workplace management system (IWMS). Prepare documentation supporting space governance reviews and approved allocation decisions. Stakeholder Engagement & Customer Service Participate in programming meetings and occupancy planning efforts for renovation and capital projects. Coordinate departmental reviews of proposed layouts and occupancy plans. Prepare and revise occupancy layouts, furniture plans, and departmental space plans using CAD software in accordance with Institute standards. Coordinate planning activities among departments, project teams, consultants, vendors, and other stakeholders to support successful project implementation and occupancy transitions. Build and maintain collaborative relationships while delivering responsive, professional, and customer-focused service. Stay informed of emerging workplace planning, space management, and higher education trends to support continuous improvement. Shift: Business Hours with weekends or evenings occasionally required Travel: Local travel between campus locations only Driving: Driving a personal vehicle for non-passenger use Starting Salary/Rate: Expected hiring range: $75,000 - $80,000 Pay transparency disclosure: The selected candidate’s salary will be determined based on factors that include the available budget, internal equity, and the final candidate’s qualifications, experience, education and other job-related credentials. This hiring range is provided as Rensselaer’s good faith estimate of the expected hiring range at the time of posting. Application instructions: Follow the on-screen prompts to create a brief online profile. Please be ready to upload your resume and cover letter. If you need assistance with the online application process, please contact careers@rpi.edu. Job Posted Date: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Total Compensation and Benefits Information: Rensselaer’s Total Compensation Program is designed to provide stable pay growth, a comprehensive and affordable benefits package, and a comprehensive and affordable retiree medical and prescription plan. Our goal is to provide you and your family with a comprehensive health and welfare program as an umbrella of financial security and protection during your employment. For more information, please visit Benefits | Human Resources (rpi.edu) . Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is committed to the cultivation of a community that is welcoming, inclusive, and above all values learning. We welcome candidates who bring a variety of perspectives to Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute's work and campus communities. Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation or gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or other characteristic protected by law. #LI-DNI Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 8c1ae71c Last Name (required) 3cc343e4 Email (required) 6d89f667 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Assistant Coach, Women's Hockey Troy, NY Athletics The duties and responsibilities of the Assistant Coach for Women’s Ice Hockey are to assist the Head Coach in the management and administration of a Division I Women’s Hockey program. The core responsibilities of the Assistant Coach are to recommend, implement and execute a successful recruiting philosophy and strategy to ensure student-athletes are committed and engaged academically, athletically, and socially. In addition, the Assistant Coach is responsible for preparing student-athletes both on and off the ice with instruction of an academic and personal nature. The Assistant Coach will also serve as coordinator for position-specific players and will assist in the development of all position players. Assistant Coach, Women's Lacrosse Troy, NY ICA Sports The Assistant Coach, Women's Lacrosse provides coaching, recruiting, and administrative support to the Head Coach in all aspects of the Women's Lacrosse program. This position assists with planning and conducting practices and competitions, instructing and mentoring student-athletes, identifying and recruiting qualified prospective student-athletes, supporting academic success, and promoting student-athlete development on and off the field. The Assistant Coach also assists with program operations, fundraising, alumni engagement, team travel, NCAA and conference compliance, and other administrative responsibilities that contribute to the success and competitiveness of the Women's Lacrosse program. Deputy Title IX Coordinator / Equal Opportunity Specialist Hybrid: in-office and remote work. Troy, NY Human Resources Office The Deputy Title IX Coordinator / Equal Opportunity Specialist supports the Institute’s commitment to an equitable, inclusive, and discrimination-free living, learning, and working environment. The position provides dedicated support for the effective administration of the Institute’s Title IX, Equal Opportunity, Title VI, and related civil rights compliance programs, helping ensure fair, thorough, and supportive processes for all participants. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert b023c25d Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories CFHE Staff Student Services and Academic Support CFHE Staff Student Services and Academic Support Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Hybrid: in-office and remote work, New York, United States Troy, NY, New York, United States Hybrid: in-office and remote work, New York, United States Troy, NY, New York, United States First Name (required) 142fcc76 Last Name (required) e16f4e8d Email (required) 2957d07b Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026 Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute (RPI) Cookie Preferences Web Privacy TileX Student Consumer Information Accessibilityy Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
