    "https://careers.rpi.edu/jobs/roofer-sr-troy-ny-new-york-united-states-80156632-2167-4f35-b78f-4d806ae12778": {
      "title": "Roofer, Sr.",
      "description": "Roofer, Sr. - Troy, NY, New York, United States Back to RPI Website My Profile Kiosk mode Roofer, Sr. Troy, NY Staff Trades, Service, and Maintenance Full Time Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary: Performs a wide range of repair and maintenance duties related to roofing and plumbing with the main focus on roofing and gutter systems. Plans and coordinates repairs of roofing systems, including but not limited to, asphalt, shingle, slate, rubber, copper, built-up and ballasted roofs. Also performs routine plumbing/heating maintenance and repair work. Participates in on-call rotation in accordance with standard operating procedures. Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma or equivalent Five (5) or more years of experience in the roofing trade Valid U.S. driver’s license Ability to be medically qualified for respirator use Relevant combinations of education, training, and experience may be considered. Preferred Qualifications: Experience working with slate roofs Minimum Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Demonstrated knowledge of roofing trade, equipment and tools Working knowledge of basic industry trades including, masonry, carpentry and metal work Ability to read, write, and perform arithmetic functions Ability to use all hand tools and operate all power tools and equipment (i.e., metal fabrication equipment, band saw, torches, power snakes, generators, compressors) Ability to work on ladders, scaffolding, and personnel lifts Ability to work in a team environment and perform independently Requires excellent customer service skills Representative Job Duties: Plan, coordinate, and oversee the installation and repair of roofing systems, including asphalt, shingle, slate, rubber, copper, and ballasted built-up roofs. Repair and waterproof skylights as needed. Install and repair pitch pockets, roof curbs, hatches, flashings, gutters, roof drains, and down leaders. Collaborate with contractors to identify and address roof problems or deficiencies as needed. Perform minor plumbing repairs, maintenance, and installation work to support campus buildings. Conduct preventative maintenance (PM) on roofing systems, gutters, and drains, working with the Shop Lead and Supervisor to develop PM procedures based on manufacturer recommendations and usage history. Shift: Standard business hours, with occasional evenings or weekends to support campus operations and maintenance needs. Travel: Local travel between campus locations only Driving: Driving a Rensselaer vehicle for non-passenger use Starting Salary/Rate: Expected hiring range: $27.00 – $32.00 per hour, with starting pay based on experience, skills, and overall fit for the role. Pay transparency disclosure: The selected candidate’s salary will be determined based on factors that include the available budget, internal equity, and the final candidate’s qualifications, experience, education and other job-related credentials. This hiring range is provided as Rensselaer’s good faith estimate of the expected hiring range at the time of posting. Application instructions: Follow the on-screen prompts to create a brief online profile. Please be ready to upload your resume and cover letter. If you need assistance with the online application process, please contact careers@rpi.edu. Job Posted Date: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Total Compensation and Benefits Information: Rensselaer’s Total Compensation Program is designed to provide stable pay growth, a comprehensive and affordable benefits package, and a comprehensive and affordable retiree medical and prescription plan. Our goal is to provide you and your family with a comprehensive health and welfare program as an umbrella of financial security and protection during your employment. For more information, please visit Benefits | Human Resources (rpi.edu) . Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is committed to the cultivation of a community that is welcoming, inclusive, and above all values learning. We welcome candidates who bring a variety of perspectives to Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute's work and campus communities. Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation or gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or other characteristic protected by law. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 537dc83f Last Name (required) 848d7a6a Email (required) 7dc377a8 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Assistant Coach, Women's Hockey Troy, NY Athletics The duties and responsibilities of the Assistant Coach for Women’s Ice Hockey are to assist the Head Coach in the management and administration of a Division I Women’s Hockey program. The core responsibilities of the Assistant Coach are to recommend, implement and execute a successful recruiting philosophy and strategy to ensure student-athletes are committed and engaged academically, athletically, and socially. In addition, the Assistant Coach is responsible for preparing student-athletes both on and off the ice with instruction of an academic and personal nature. The Assistant Coach will also serve as coordinator for position-specific players and will assist in the development of all position players. Assistant Coach, Women's Lacrosse Troy, NY ICA Sports The Assistant Coach, Women's Lacrosse provides coaching, recruiting, and administrative support to the Head Coach in all aspects of the Women's Lacrosse program. This position assists with planning and conducting practices and competitions, instructing and mentoring student-athletes, identifying and recruiting qualified prospective student-athletes, supporting academic success, and promoting student-athlete development on and off the field. The Assistant Coach also assists with program operations, fundraising, alumni engagement, team travel, NCAA and conference compliance, and other administrative responsibilities that contribute to the success and competitiveness of the Women's Lacrosse program. Deputy Title IX Coordinator / Equal Opportunity Specialist Hybrid: in-office and remote work. Troy, NY Human Resources Office The Deputy Title IX Coordinator / Equal Opportunity Specialist supports the Institute’s commitment to an equitable, inclusive, and discrimination-free living, learning, and working environment. The position provides dedicated support for the effective administration of the Institute’s Title IX, Equal Opportunity, Title VI, and related civil rights compliance programs, helping ensure fair, thorough, and supportive processes for all participants. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 24ecb30e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Staff Trades, Service, and Maintenance Staff Trades, Service, and Maintenance Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Troy, NY, New York, United States Troy, NY, New York, United States First Name (required) 8c159721 Last Name (required) 93a64d24 Email (required) 7840f90d Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026 Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute (RPI) Cookie Preferences Web Privacy TileX Student Consumer Information Accessibilityy Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
