    "https://careers.rpi.edu/jobs/operating-mechanic-troy-ny-new-york-united-states-c46ab955-e016-4110-9436-faae3e7b0299": {
      "title": "Operating Mechanic",
      "description": "Operating Mechanic - Troy, NY, New York, United States Back to RPI Website My Profile Kiosk mode Operating Mechanic Troy, NY Staff Trades, Service, and Maintenance Full Time Add to favorites View favorites Who we are Why Rensselaer? Nestled on a beautiful 275-acre campus in upstate NY, Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is home to five schools, 32 research centers, three makerspaces, an observatory, one of the world’s fastest supercomputers, and the IBM Quantum System One - the first university-based quantum computer in the world. With top notch employee health and retirement benefits, Rensselaer offers its full-time employees a generous paid time off program, tuition remission, and opportunities for career growth. Job Summary Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is seeking qualified candidates for Operating Mechanic and / or Senior Operating Mechanic positions within our steam plant operations. These positions perform maintenance and repairs on steam boilers and steam plant auxiliaries, working in a rotation to operate two central steam plants. Both levels provide maintenance and repair response coverage on evening, night, and weekend shifts for all campus facilities. Minimum Qualifications Operating Mechanic High school diploma or equivalent One (1) year of experience maintaining commercial or industrial mechanical equipment preferred Valid U.S. driver’s license Senior Operating Mechanic High school diploma or equivalent Five (5) years of experience maintaining and operating a steam plant or comparable industrial facility Valid U.S. driver’s license Applicants must meet the stated minimum education and experience requirements for the level they wish to be considered. Minimum Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities For Both Levels: Working knowledge of stem cycle, plumbing, piping, mechanical repairs, electrical work, and general construction Ability to interpret technical drawings and documentation Strong communication and customer service skills Flexibility in dealing with emergency situations Basic computer skills and familiarity with Microsoft Windows Constant attention to safety for self, co-workers, and others In addition, Senior Operating Mechanic candidates must demonstrate: Thorough knowledge of steam plant operations, boiler systems, and associated chemicals Ability to independently operate, troubleshoot, and maintain complex plant systems Experience planning and scheduling maintenance activities Ability to assume lead responsibilities in the absence of a supervisor or lead mechanic Job Duties Operating Mechanic: Monitor steam plant operations for safe, reliable, and efficient performance as instructed Start/stop boilers and auxiliary equipment and switch boiler fuels when instructed Maintain and update operational logs and reports Receive oil deliveries in accordance with Institute policies and applicable regulations Conduct water tests and adjust chemical feed rates as directed Perform routine and emergency maintenance on mechanical, piping, electrical, and instrumentation components Assist with annual high-pressure boiler shutdowns and maintenance inspections Monitor and maintain chemical inventories, move chemicals and salt as needed Check and service satellite steam boilers and closed loop systems across campus Perform other duties as assigned Senior Operating Mechanic (includes all duties above, plus): Independently start, stop, and troubleshoot boilers and auxiliary systems without supervision Identify maintenance needs and work with supervisor to plan and schedule repairs Conduct and interpret water tests, adjusting chemical systems proactively Provide quality control oversight during annual high-pressure boiler shutdowns Order supplies and materials for approval by the Lead Operating Mechanic or Supervisor Assume lead responsibilities when Supervisor or Lead Operating Mechanic is unavailable Shift Non-Standard Shift: This position involves scheduled shift assignments on the 1st, 2nd, and 3rd shifts. The 3rd shift is typically scheduled only during the winter months, generally from December through late March, depending on weather conditions and the onset of freezing temperatures. The role supports the operation of two central steam plants and provides maintenance and repair response coverage for all campus facilities. Travel Local travel between campus locations only Driving Driving a Rensselaer vehicle for non-passenger use Starting Salary/Rate Expected hiring range: Operating Mechanic: $26.00 - $28.50 per hour Sr. Operating Mechanic: $29.00 - 30.00 per hour Pay transparency disclosure: The selected candidate’s salary will be determined based on factors that include the available budget, internal equity, and the final candidate’s qualifications, experience, education and other job-related credentials. This hiring range is provided as Rensselaer’s good faith estimate of the expected hiring range at the time of posting. Application instructions Follow the on-screen prompts to create a brief online profile. Please be ready to upload your resume and cover letter. If you need assistance with the online application process, please contact careers@rpi.edu. Job Posted Date Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Total Compensation and Benefits Information Rensselaer’s Total Compensation Program is designed to provide stable pay growth, a comprehensive and affordable benefits package, and a comprehensive and affordable retiree medical and prescription plan. Our goal is to provide you and your family with a comprehensive health and welfare program as an umbrella of financial security and protection during your employment. For more information, please visit Benefits | Human Resources (rpi.edu) . Rensselaer is committed to the cultivation of a community that is welcoming, inclusive, and above all values learning. We welcome candidates who bring a variety of perspectives to Rensselaer’s work and campus communities. Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation or gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or other characteristic protected by law. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 03d0a9bd Last Name (required) b76a7440 Email (required) b5870e8f Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Assistant Coach, Women's Hockey Troy, NY Athletics The duties and responsibilities of the Assistant Coach for Women’s Ice Hockey are to assist the Head Coach in the management and administration of a Division I Women’s Hockey program. The core responsibilities of the Assistant Coach are to recommend, implement and execute a successful recruiting philosophy and strategy to ensure student-athletes are committed and engaged academically, athletically, and socially. In addition, the Assistant Coach is responsible for preparing student-athletes both on and off the ice with instruction of an academic and personal nature. The Assistant Coach will also serve as coordinator for position-specific players and will assist in the development of all position players. Assistant Coach, Women's Lacrosse Troy, NY ICA Sports The Assistant Coach, Women's Lacrosse provides coaching, recruiting, and administrative support to the Head Coach in all aspects of the Women's Lacrosse program. This position assists with planning and conducting practices and competitions, instructing and mentoring student-athletes, identifying and recruiting qualified prospective student-athletes, supporting academic success, and promoting student-athlete development on and off the field. The Assistant Coach also assists with program operations, fundraising, alumni engagement, team travel, NCAA and conference compliance, and other administrative responsibilities that contribute to the success and competitiveness of the Women's Lacrosse program. Deputy Title IX Coordinator / Equal Opportunity Specialist Hybrid: in-office and remote work. Troy, NY Human Resources Office The Deputy Title IX Coordinator / Equal Opportunity Specialist supports the Institute’s commitment to an equitable, inclusive, and discrimination-free living, learning, and working environment. The position provides dedicated support for the effective administration of the Institute’s Title IX, Equal Opportunity, Title VI, and related civil rights compliance programs, helping ensure fair, thorough, and supportive processes for all participants. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 5d53426b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Staff Trades, Service, and Maintenance Staff Trades, Service, and Maintenance Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Troy, NY, New York, United States Troy, NY, New York, United States First Name (required) e8cddb9d Last Name (required) f6a7fcae Email (required) f33a3170 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026 Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute (RPI) Cookie Preferences Web Privacy TileX Student Consumer Information Accessibilityy Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
