    "https://careers.rpi.edu/jobs/public-safety-communications-specialist-troy-ny-new-york-united-states-cdadb3df-2bc1-41c6-a26e-0eb8b5b8a351": {
      "title": "Public Safety Communications Specialist",
      "description": "Public Safety Communications Specialist - Troy, NY, New York, United States Back to RPI Website My Profile Kiosk mode Public Safety Communications Specialist Troy, NY Public Safety Staff Full Time Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary: The Public Safety Communications Specialist is responsible for monitoring, responding, and taking appropriate actions for incoming calls for service; process emergency and non-emergency communications, multi-agency radio communications, and provide documentation for these incidents in support of Public Safety operations. This position also serves as the focal point for all Institute communications outside normal business hours Who we are: Founded in 1824, Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute (RPI) is the first technological research university in the United States. We bring creativity, science, and technology together to address society's greatest challenges. We cultivate exceptional problem-solvers by immersing them in a culture of rigorous inquiry, disciplined practice, and hands-on application. Our strategic plan, RPI Forward, charts a pioneering course for the next era of RPI. Explore the RPI Forward plan. ↗︎ Nestled on a beautiful 275-acre campus in upstate NY, RPI is home to five schools, 32 research centers, three makerspaces, an observatory, one of the world’s fastest supercomputers, and the IBM Quantum System One - the first university-based quantum computer in the world. With top notch employee health and retirement benefits, RPI offers its full-time employees a generous paid time off program, tuition remission, and opportunities for career growth. Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma or equivalent required Experience: Minimum of three (3) years of customer service experience, or an equivalent combination of education, training, and related experience Requirements: Ability to obtain and maintain a New York State Security Guard License Subject to criminal history check, background investigation, and physical examination Relevant combinations of education, training, and experience will be considered. Preferred Qualifications: Education: Some college coursework required (minimum of 30 college credits) Experience: Experience in a dispatching or call center role preferred Minimum Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Requires ability to multi-task during multiple emergency situations Requires excellent customer relation skills Ability to work under pressure in a fast paced environment Demonstrated knowledge and proficiency in the use of computer based systems Must be detailed oriented Requires the ability to process and prioritize simultaneous situations Clear and effective verbal and written communication skills Must be available for flexible shift scheduling Representative Job Duties: Answer and document all telephone and multi-agency radio communications; take appropriate action based on the nature of the call. Prioritize and process all calls for service and conduct notifications as required to ensure prompt dispatch of personnel. Monitor duty locations and officer status during critical incidents. Provide additional resources, including dispatching personnel, equipment, and emergency response services as needed. Monitor and operate all electronic security systems. Dispatch appropriate resources to respond to alarms at various on- and off-campus locations based on received data. Coordinate and respond to requests for eJustice services, including but not limited to DMV information, entering data for lost or stolen property, missing persons, wanted persons, and required training notifications from DCJS. Perform emergency dispatch and notifications via radio, telephone, or pager for emergency personnel response teams for fire, intrusion, life-safety, and medical incidents. Coordinate emergency response services, including City of Troy emergency services and internal notification and response. Provide incident-specific briefings for RPI administrators as requested. Effectively manage and respond to simultaneous requests for service. Conduct inter-shift briefings with relief shifts, including updates on activities and the status of unresolved matters from the previous shift. Enter data into the Computer Aided Dispatch (CAD) system for all calls for service for supervisory review and records management. File and forward reports as appropriate. Assign, distribute, and collect department and RPI equipment for various departments within the RPI community and authorized vendors (e.g., keys, access cards, radios, patrol vehicles). Return equipment to proper storage areas or departments as appropriate. Provide telephone and walk-in information assistance and route department and RPI calls (including backup support to the Institute Operator after regular business hours). Provide campus and local directions and general information. After normal business hours, provide emergency replacement of access cards as required via the Access Control System. Perform other duties as assigned. Shift: Public Safety: Various Shifts.  All members of the Department of Public Safety must be available for flexible shift scheduling Including: 3rd shift 11:00 PM - 7:00 AM 2nd Shift 3:00 PM - 11:00 PM 1st Shift 7:00 AM - 3:00 PM Travel: Local travel between campus locations only Starting Salary/Rate: Expected hiring range: $20.00 Pay transparency disclosure: The selected candidate’s salary will be determined based on factors that include the available budget, internal equity, and the final candidate’s qualifications, experience, education and other job-related credentials. This hiring range is provided as Rensselaer’s good faith estimate of the expected hiring range at the time of posting. Application instructions: Follow the on-screen prompts to create a brief online profile. Please be ready to upload your resume and cover letter. If you need assistance with the online application process, please contact careers@rpi.edu. Job Posted Date: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Total Compensation and Benefits Information: RPI's Total Compensation Program is designed to provide stable pay growth, a comprehensive and affordable benefits package, and a comprehensive and affordable retiree medical and prescription plan. Our goal is to provide you and your family with a comprehensive health and welfare program as an umbrella of financial security and protection during your employment. For more information, please visit Benefits | Human Resources (rpi.edu) . Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is committed to the cultivation of a community that is welcoming, inclusive, and above all values learning. We welcome candidates who bring a variety of perspectives to Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute's work and campus communities. Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation or gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or other characteristic protected by law. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) f2bfbe17 Last Name (required) fc4b8f9d Email (required) 99728be1 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Assistant Coach, Women's Hockey Troy, NY Athletics The duties and responsibilities of the Assistant Coach for Women’s Ice Hockey are to assist the Head Coach in the management and administration of a Division I Women’s Hockey program. The core responsibilities of the Assistant Coach are to recommend, implement and execute a successful recruiting philosophy and strategy to ensure student-athletes are committed and engaged academically, athletically, and socially. In addition, the Assistant Coach is responsible for preparing student-athletes both on and off the ice with instruction of an academic and personal nature. The Assistant Coach will also serve as coordinator for position-specific players and will assist in the development of all position players. Assistant Coach, Women's Lacrosse Troy, NY ICA Sports The Assistant Coach, Women's Lacrosse provides coaching, recruiting, and administrative support to the Head Coach in all aspects of the Women's Lacrosse program. This position assists with planning and conducting practices and competitions, instructing and mentoring student-athletes, identifying and recruiting qualified prospective student-athletes, supporting academic success, and promoting student-athlete development on and off the field. The Assistant Coach also assists with program operations, fundraising, alumni engagement, team travel, NCAA and conference compliance, and other administrative responsibilities that contribute to the success and competitiveness of the Women's Lacrosse program. Deputy Title IX Coordinator / Equal Opportunity Specialist Hybrid: in-office and remote work. Troy, NY Human Resources Office The Deputy Title IX Coordinator / Equal Opportunity Specialist supports the Institute’s commitment to an equitable, inclusive, and discrimination-free living, learning, and working environment. The position provides dedicated support for the effective administration of the Institute’s Title IX, Equal Opportunity, Title VI, and related civil rights compliance programs, helping ensure fair, thorough, and supportive processes for all participants. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert bd104f53 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Public Safety Staff Public Safety Staff Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Troy, NY, New York, United States Troy, NY, New York, United States First Name (required) 16c04d89 Last Name (required) 96fe549e Email (required) 7c8ffc19 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026 Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute (RPI) Cookie Preferences Web Privacy TileX Student Consumer Information Accessibilityy Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
