    "https://careers.rpi.edu/jobs/assistant-vice-provost-undergraduate-admissions-troy-ny-new-york-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Vice Provost, Undergraduate Admissions",
      "description": "Assistant Vice Provost, Undergraduate Admissions - Troy, NY, New York, United States Back to RPI Website My Profile Kiosk mode Assistant Vice Provost, Undergraduate Admissions Troy, NY Business, Accounting and Finance CFHE Staff Student Services and Academic Support Show More Show Less Full Time Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary: The Assistant Vice Provost for Undergraduate Admissions leads the full undergraduate admissions operation and sets the strategy for recruiting and enrolling each entering class. The position directs about thirty staff across recruitment, transfer, international, campus engagement, and operations, manages the recruitment and visit budgets, and carries a central share of responsibility for net tuition revenue, the largest single part of the operating budget. Reporting to the Vice Provost for Enrollment Management, the Assistant Vice Provost provides the analytics, technology, and yield leadership that recruitment now requires in a contracting market, and works as a peer with the academic deans, the marketing office, and the financial aid office. Who we are: Founded in 1824, Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute (RPI) is the first technological research university in the United States. We bring creativity, science, and technology together to address society's greatest challenges. We cultivate exceptional problem-solvers by immersing them in a culture of rigorous inquiry, disciplined practice, and hands-on application. Our strategic plan, RPI Forward, charts a pioneering course for the next era of RPI. Explore the RPI Forward plan. ↗︎ Nestled on a beautiful 275-acre campus in upstate NY, RPI is home to five schools, 32 research centers, three makerspaces, an observatory, one of the world’s fastest supercomputers, and the IBM Quantum System One - the first university-based quantum computer in the world. With top notch employee health and retirement benefits, Rensselaer offers its full-time employees a generous paid time off program, tuition remission, and opportunities for career growth. Minimum Qualifications: Education Master's degree required. Experience Minimum of eight (8) years of progressively responsible experience in undergraduate admissions, enrollment management, or a related higher education field. Minimum of five (5) years of supervisory experience leading professional staff and strategic enrollment initiatives. Demonstrated success developing and implementing enrollment strategies that achieve recruitment, admission, and enrollment goals. Relevant combinations of education, training and experience may be considered. Preferred Qualifications: Experience working at an R1 research university, preferably with a strong science and technology focus. Experience leading or supporting transfer and international student recruitment, as well as developing and managing campus visit, admissions event, and yield programs designed to support enrollment goals. Minimum Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Knowledge of enrollment management principles, including recruitment, admissions, financial aid, and student success strategies. Knowledge of higher education policies, regulations, and best practices related to enrollment and student services. Strong leadership and personnel management skills, with the ability to recruit, develop, mentor, and evaluate staff across multifunctional teams. Ability to lead organizational change initiatives and effectively manage competing priorities in a dynamic environment. Strong budget development, fiscal management, and resource allocation skills. Demonstrated expertise in data analytics, including predictive and prescriptive modeling, statistical analysis, and data visualization to support enrollment strategy and institutional decision-making. Ability to interpret complex data and translate findings into actionable recommendations for executive leadership. Excellent strategic planning, project management, and organizational skills. Strong collaboration and relationship-building skills with academic departments, administrative units, and external stakeholders. Exceptional written, verbal, and presentation communication skills. Ability to influence, negotiate, and build consensus across diverse constituencies. Proficiency with student information systems (SIS), customer relationship management (CRM) systems, enrollment management technologies, and business intelligence/reporting tools. Ability to maintain confidentiality and exercise sound judgment in handling sensitive student and institutional information. Commitment to fostering an inclusive, student-centered environment and promoting continuous improvement through innovation and data-informed practices. Representative Job Duties: Set and execute a comprehensive recruitment and yield strategy for first-year and transfer classes. Lead the functional areas of the office, including first-year recruitment, transfer recruitment, international recruitment and global partnerships, campus engagement and visit experience, and operations. Direct the use of predictive and prescriptive analytics to guide territory management, communication strategies, financial aid leveraging, and yield decisions. Manage recruitment and campus visit budgets while ensuring responsible stewardship of net tuition revenue. Oversee the customer relationship management (CRM) system and related enrollment technologies, including artificial intelligence tools and financial aid optimization platforms. Partner with academic deans, marketing, financial aid, and student affairs to align recruitment strategies with institutional goals. Build, develop, and lead a high-performing, multifunctional team while guiding the office through organizational, structural, and process improvements. Represent Undergraduate Admissions to institutional leadership and external partners. Shift: This position primarily works standard business hours, Monday through Friday. Periodic evening and weekend hours are required to support recruitment events, campus visit programs, open houses, admitted student programs, yield activities, and other institutional events. Additional hours may be required during peak recruitment and enrollment periods. Travel: Periodic Overnight Travel (Up to 25%) Periodic travel is required to represent the Institute at recruitment events, college fairs, high schools, community colleges, professional conferences, and other enrollment-related activities. Travel may include local, regional, national, and occasional international recruitment, as well as visits to partner organizations and institutions. Overnight, evening, and weekend travel may be required during peak recruitment cycles. Driving: Incidental driving possible, but not required Starting Salary/Rate: Expected hiring range: $170,000 - $210,000 Pay transparency disclosure: The selected candidate’s salary will be determined based on factors that include the available budget, internal equity, and the final candidate’s qualifications, experience, education and other job-related credentials. This hiring range is provided as Rensselaer’s good faith estimate of the expected hiring range at the time of posting. Application instructions: Follow the on-screen prompts to create a brief online profile. Please be ready to upload your resume and cover letter. If you need assistance with the online application process, please contact careers@rpi.edu. Job Posted Date: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Total Compensation and Benefits Information: Rensselaer’s Total Compensation Program is designed to provide stable pay growth, a comprehensive and affordable benefits package, and a comprehensive and affordable retiree medical and prescription plan. Our goal is to provide you and your family with a comprehensive health and welfare program as an umbrella of financial security and protection during your employment. For more information, please visit Benefits | Human Resources (rpi.edu) . Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is committed to the cultivation of a community that is welcoming, inclusive, and above all values learning. We welcome candidates who bring a variety of perspectives to Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute's work and campus communities. Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation or gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or other characteristic protected by law. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 24d6a64a Last Name (required) 03de11fc Email (required) d988a70e Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Assistant Coach, Women's Hockey Troy, NY Athletics The duties and responsibilities of the Assistant Coach for Women’s Ice Hockey are to assist the Head Coach in the management and administration of a Division I Women’s Hockey program. The core responsibilities of the Assistant Coach are to recommend, implement and execute a successful recruiting philosophy and strategy to ensure student-athletes are committed and engaged academically, athletically, and socially. In addition, the Assistant Coach is responsible for preparing student-athletes both on and off the ice with instruction of an academic and personal nature. The Assistant Coach will also serve as coordinator for position-specific players and will assist in the development of all position players. Assistant Coach, Women's Lacrosse Troy, NY ICA Sports The Assistant Coach, Women's Lacrosse provides coaching, recruiting, and administrative support to the Head Coach in all aspects of the Women's Lacrosse program. This position assists with planning and conducting practices and competitions, instructing and mentoring student-athletes, identifying and recruiting qualified prospective student-athletes, supporting academic success, and promoting student-athlete development on and off the field. The Assistant Coach also assists with program operations, fundraising, alumni engagement, team travel, NCAA and conference compliance, and other administrative responsibilities that contribute to the success and competitiveness of the Women's Lacrosse program. Deputy Title IX Coordinator / Equal Opportunity Specialist Hybrid: in-office and remote work. Troy, NY Human Resources Office The Deputy Title IX Coordinator / Equal Opportunity Specialist supports the Institute’s commitment to an equitable, inclusive, and discrimination-free living, learning, and working environment. The position provides dedicated support for the effective administration of the Institute’s Title IX, Equal Opportunity, Title VI, and related civil rights compliance programs, helping ensure fair, thorough, and supportive processes for all participants. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 476d52fc Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Business, Accounting and Finance CFHE Staff Student Services and Academic Support Business, Accounting and Finance CFHE Staff Student Services and Academic Support Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Troy, NY, New York, United States Troy, NY, New York, United States First Name (required) 431acca0 Last Name (required) 1a182771 Email (required) 3a436518 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026 Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute (RPI) Cookie Preferences Web Privacy TileX Student Consumer Information Accessibilityy Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
