    "https://careers.rpi.edu/jobs/repairer-troy-ny-new-york-united-states": {
      "title": "Repairer",
      "description": "Repairer - Troy, NY, New York, United States Back to RPI Website My Profile Kiosk mode Repairer Troy, NY Staff Trades, Service, and Maintenance Full Time Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary: The Repairer performs basic repair and maintenance assignments on facilities and equipment using a variety of trades such as, but not limited to, carpentry, mechanical, electrical, plumbing, painting, and masonry. Also works as a part of a team to complete larger scale renovations. This position participates in on-call rotation for off-hour repairs in academic and residential buildings. Who we are: Founded in 1824, Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute (RPI) is the first technological research university in the United States. We bring creativity, science, and technology together to address society's greatest challenges. We cultivate exceptional problem-solvers by immersing them in a culture of rigorous inquiry, disciplined practice, and hands-on application. Our strategic plan, RPI Forward, charts a pioneering course for the next era of RPI. Explore the RPI Forward plan. ↗︎ Nestled on a beautiful 275-acre campus in upstate NY, RPI is home to five schools, 32 research centers, three makerspaces, an observatory, one of the world’s fastest supercomputers, and the IBM Quantum System One - the first university-based quantum computer in the world. With top notch employee health and retirement benefits, Rensselaer offers its full-time employees a generous paid time off program, tuition remission, and opportunities for career growth. Minimum Qualifications: HS diploma or equivalent One (1) year experience in construction, facilities maintenance or related field Valid US driver’s license Applicants must meet stated minimum education and experience requirements. Minimum Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Knowledge of basic construction trades including carpentry, plumbing, electrical, and metal work Ability to read, write, and perform simple use of arithmetic Ability to follow instructions and perform with minimal direct supervision Ability to use all hand tools and operate all basic power tools and equipment Ability to work in a team environment and perform basic tasks independently Must have the ability to use a personal computer (Outlook and job specific software) Excellent customer service skills Representative Job Duties: Performs basic repairs in a variety of areas including carpentry, mechanical, electrical, plumbing, painting, masonry, minor glass repair, minor metal work, and related maintenance areas. Works with Senior Repairers and the Supervisor to fabricate and rework parts for equipment that are no longer available or are obsolete. Performs scheduled preventive maintenance on a wide range of equipment and facilities in assigned areas, including but not limited to filter changes, battery replacements, safety shower inspections, door hardware maintenance, and fan coil cleaning. Completes repair and maintenance assignments according to work orders and instructions. Records maintenance information for entry into the computerized maintenance management system (CMMS). Provides the Supervisor with a list of materials required for assigned tasks and may transport materials to and from job sites. Assists with complex repair and maintenance assignments under the direction of Senior Repairers and trade shop personnel. Repairs or replaces appliances, including stoves, refrigerators, water heaters, and air conditioners. Winterizes windows and window air conditioning units as required. Works with trade shop personnel and Senior Repairers to refurbish bathrooms and kitchens. Provides set-up services for campus events and functions, including but not limited to student orientation, daycare, and commencement activities. Loads and unloads trucks, moves furniture, cleans out apartments and offices, removes litter and discarded materials, and sets up or takes down furniture to support room use transitions. Repairs and maintains shop equipment. Maintains equipment, supplies, and work areas in a clean and orderly condition and returns equipment, tools, and materials to the appropriate storage locations. Reports work coordination issues, technical concerns, communication needs, tool, equipment, or key issues, and scheduling concerns to the Supervisor. Reports maintenance issues through FIXX to ensure work orders are generated for repairs that fall outside the scope of assigned responsibilities and require support from other shops or departments. Installs and repairs campus signage as assigned. Shift: Business Hours with weekends or evenings occasionally required Travel: Local travel between campus locations only Driving: Driving a personal vehicle for non-passenger use Starting Salary/Rate: Expected hiring range: $21.00 - $22.50 Pay transparency disclosure: The selected candidate’s salary will be determined based on factors that include the available budget, internal equity, and the final candidate’s qualifications, experience, education and other job-related credentials. This hiring range is provided as Rensselaer’s good faith estimate of the expected hiring range at the time of posting. Application instructions: Follow the on-screen prompts to create a brief online profile. Please be ready to upload your resume and cover letter. If you need assistance with the online application process, please contact careers@rpi.edu. Job Posted Date: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Total Compensation and Benefits Information: Rensselaer’s Total Compensation Program is designed to provide stable pay growth, a comprehensive and affordable benefits package, and a comprehensive and affordable retiree medical and prescription plan. Our goal is to provide you and your family with a comprehensive health and welfare program as an umbrella of financial security and protection during your employment. For more information, please visit Benefits | Human Resources (rpi.edu) . Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is committed to the cultivation of a community that is welcoming, inclusive, and above all values learning. We welcome candidates who bring a variety of perspectives to Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute's work and campus communities. Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation or gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or other characteristic protected by law. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 49aafd1a Last Name (required) 691cbcd5 Email (required) a6fa04b4 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Assistant Coach, Women's Hockey Troy, NY Athletics The duties and responsibilities of the Assistant Coach for Women’s Ice Hockey are to assist the Head Coach in the management and administration of a Division I Women’s Hockey program. The core responsibilities of the Assistant Coach are to recommend, implement and execute a successful recruiting philosophy and strategy to ensure student-athletes are committed and engaged academically, athletically, and socially. In addition, the Assistant Coach is responsible for preparing student-athletes both on and off the ice with instruction of an academic and personal nature. The Assistant Coach will also serve as coordinator for position-specific players and will assist in the development of all position players. Assistant Coach, Women's Lacrosse Troy, NY ICA Sports The Assistant Coach, Women's Lacrosse provides coaching, recruiting, and administrative support to the Head Coach in all aspects of the Women's Lacrosse program. This position assists with planning and conducting practices and competitions, instructing and mentoring student-athletes, identifying and recruiting qualified prospective student-athletes, supporting academic success, and promoting student-athlete development on and off the field. The Assistant Coach also assists with program operations, fundraising, alumni engagement, team travel, NCAA and conference compliance, and other administrative responsibilities that contribute to the success and competitiveness of the Women's Lacrosse program. Deputy Title IX Coordinator / Equal Opportunity Specialist Hybrid: in-office and remote work. Troy, NY Human Resources Office The Deputy Title IX Coordinator / Equal Opportunity Specialist supports the Institute’s commitment to an equitable, inclusive, and discrimination-free living, learning, and working environment. The position provides dedicated support for the effective administration of the Institute’s Title IX, Equal Opportunity, Title VI, and related civil rights compliance programs, helping ensure fair, thorough, and supportive processes for all participants. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 0921863a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Staff Trades, Service, and Maintenance Staff Trades, Service, and Maintenance Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Troy, NY, New York, United States Troy, NY, New York, United States First Name (required) 85a2540f Last Name (required) 65e149a1 Email (required) 3dcae6d6 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026 Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute (RPI) Cookie Preferences Web Privacy TileX Student Consumer Information Accessibilityy Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please 