al, Financial) Microelectronics has played a significant role in nearly every major technological development of the last half-century. In keeping with our creative, interdisciplinary reputation for innovation, Rensselaer researchers cover the whole semiconductor spectrum, from theory to practice to product and from bench to bedside, across materials, design, devices, and systems. Please visit chips.rpi.edu for more information. The Office for Research collaborates with important external partners in the federal and state government, foundations and in industry to expand the impact our work and to support our world-class researchers as they improve lives, advance society, and change the world. Rensselaer faculty and alumni include more than 145 National Academy members, six members of the National Inventors Hall of Fame, six National Medal of Technology winners, five National Medal of Science winners, # astronauts, and a Nobel Prize winner in Physics. With nearly 200 years of experience advancing scientific and technological knowledge, Rensselaer remains focused on addressing global challenges with a spirit of ingenuity and collaboration. To learn more, please visit www.rpi.edu . Are you ready to change the world? Apply now! Job summary Some of the areas that may be hiring researchers and research support positions in the area of Microelectronics include: Materials & Metrology Hardware Co-design Computational Microelectronics Hetero-integration Note: The availability of positions is dependent on the availability of sponsored funding. Not all areas will have all positions, and some areas may be fully staffed. Qualifications Postdoctoral Research Associate - Candidates must have finished all requirements for their PhD or foreign equivalent at the beginning of their appointment Research Associate or (Sr.) Research Scientist - Opportunities exist for those with a relevant advanced degree, publication record, and/or significant additional years of paid professional experience in a related position. Individuals who possess these qualifications and who have the potential to, or a demonstrated track record of being able to build collaborative external partnerships are especially desirable (Sr.) Research Specialist - Positions require a relevant bachelor's degree / foreign equivalent or higher (Sr.) Research Engineer - Research Assistant - candidates must possess an associate's degree / foreign equivalent or relevant combination of experience, education and training Pay transparency Pay transparency disclosure: The actual salary/wage that is provided to selected candidates will be determined based on factors that include the available budget, internal equity, and the needs of the department, and the final candidate’s qualifications, experience, education, and other job-related credentials. The following hiring ranges are provided as Rensselaer’s good faith estimate of the expected hiring range at the time of posting. Postdoctoral Research Associate: $62,354 - $65,000 / yr Research Associate: $64,000 - $66,000 / yr Research Scientist: $66,000 - $95,000 / yr Sr. Research Scientist: $80,000 - $138,000 / yr *** Research Specialist: $18.00 - $26.44 / hr Sr. Research Specialist: $62,354 - 66,000 / yr *** Research Engineer: $66,000 - $86,000 / yr Sr. Research Engineer: $87,000 – $95,000 / yr *** Research Assistant: $16.00 - $22.00 / hr Application instructions Follow the on-screen prompts to create an application. Please be ready to upload any required documents, such as your resume and cover letter If you need assistance with the online application process, please contact careers@rpi.edu Job posted date Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Total Compensation and Benefits Information Rensselaer’s Total Compensation Program is designed to provide stable pay growth, a comprehensive and affordable benefits package, and a comprehensive and affordable retiree medical and prescription plan. Rensselaer is recognized locally and nationally for the depth and breadth of its compensation and benefits program. Our goal is to provide you and your family with a comprehensive health and welfare program as an umbrella of financial security and protection during your employment. For more information, please visit Benefits | Human Resources (rpi.edu) . Rensselaer is committed to the cultivation of a community that is welcoming, inclusive, and above all values learning. We welcome candidates who bring a variety of perspectives to Rensselaer’s work and campus communities. Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation or gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or other characteristic protected by law. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) bccc5c6c Last Name (required) d814e121 Email (required) 1dcf7f01 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Assistant Coach, Women's Hockey Troy, NY Athletics The duties and responsibilities of the Assistant Coach for Women’s Ice Hockey are to assist the Head Coach in the management and administration of a Division I Women’s Hockey program. The core responsibilities of the Assistant Coach are to recommend, implement and execute a successful recruiting philosophy and strategy to ensure student-athletes are committed and engaged academically, athletically, and socially. In addition, the Assistant Coach is responsible for preparing student-athletes both on and off the ice with instruction of an academic and personal nature. The Assistant Coach will also serve as coordinator for position-specific players and will assist in the development of all position players. Assistant Coach, Women's Lacrosse Troy, NY ICA Sports The Assistant Coach, Women's Lacrosse provides coaching, recruiting, and administrative support to the Head Coach in all aspects of the Women's Lacrosse program. This position assists with planning and conducting practices and competitions, instructing and mentoring student-athletes, identifying and recruiting qualified prospective student-athletes, supporting academic success, and promoting student-athlete development on and off the field. The Assistant Coach also assists with program operations, fundraising, alumni engagement, team travel, NCAA and conference compliance, and other administrative responsibilities that contribute to the success and competitiveness of the Women's Lacrosse program. Deputy Title IX Coordinator / Equal Opportunity Specialist Hybrid: in-office and remote work. Troy, NY Human Resources Office The Deputy Title IX Coordinator / Equal Opportunity Specialist supports the Institute’s commitment to an equitable, inclusive, and discrimination-free living, learning, and working environment. The position provides dedicated support for the effective administration of the Institute’s Title IX, Equal Opportunity, Title VI, and related civil rights compliance programs, helping ensure fair, thorough, and supportive processes for all participants. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 8d18387e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Research: Microelectronics Researchers and Research Support Research: Microelectronics Researchers and Research Support Employment Type Full Time Part Time Seasonal or Temporary Full Time Part Time Seasonal or Temporary Locations Troy, NY, New York, United States Troy, NY, New York, United States First Name (required) cb406c8e Last Name (required) ce07540e Email (required) f6161b56 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026 Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute (RPI) Cookie Preferences Web Privacy TileX Student Consumer Information Ac