    "https://careers.rpi.edu/jobs/administrative-coordinator-troy-ny-new-york-united-states-72a53f77-ed1d-4b9f-99fc-46e71083c686": {
      "title": "Administrative Coordinator",
      "description": "Administrative Coordinator - Troy, NY, New York, United States Back to RPI Website My Profile Kiosk mode Administrative Coordinator Troy, NY Administrative Support Staff Full Time Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary: The Administrative Coordinator supports the strategic and operational effectiveness of the School of Humanities, Arts, and Social Sciences (HASS) by working closely with the Manager of Administrative Operations and Department Heads. This position provides administrative coordination across HASS departments, ensuring the smooth delivery of department-level operations, initiatives, and priorities. Reporting directly to the Manager of Administrative Operations, the Administrative Coordinator plays an integral role in executing the Manager’s direction and priorities at the school- and department-level. While supporting Department Heads in their academic and administrative responsibilities, the Coordinator's work is guided by school-wide goals and coordinated through the Manager. This position focuses on the efficient functioning of departments as organizational units. The Coordinator’s responsibilities prioritize administrative planning, process improvement, and coordination of academic and research-related activities. Who we are: Founded in 1824, Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute (RPI) is the first technological research university in the United States. We bring creativity, science, and technology together to address society's greatest challenges. We cultivate exceptional problem-solvers by immersing them in a culture of rigorous inquiry, disciplined practice, and hands-on application. Our strategic plan, RPI Forward, charts a pioneering course for the next era of RPI. Explore the RPI Forward plan. ↗︎ Nestled on a beautiful 275-acre campus in upstate NY, RPI is home to five schools, 32 research centers, three makerspaces, an observatory, one of the world’s fastest supercomputers, and the IBM Quantum System One - the first university-based quantum computer in the world. With top notch employee health and retirement benefits, Rensselaer offers its full-time employees a generous paid time off program, tuition remission, and opportunities for career growth. Minimum Qualifications: Associate's Degree in applicable field and two (2) or more years of directly related experience. Additional directly related experience may be substituted for the degree. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in higher education Minimum Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Ability to work with minimum supervision and independently but also as part of a team Excellent communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills Ability to compose correspondence and reports Requires good problem solving skills involving multiple variables in complex situations Must possess the skills necessary to deliver exemplary customer service Demonstrated proficiency in MS Office (word, excel, access, Outlook) Ability to prioritize work and to handle several tasks simultaneously Ability to perform basic financial functions Ability to work in fast paced environment Strong attention to detail Representative Job Duties: Department Operations Oversight: Coordinate and monitor the daily operational functions of assigned departments, implementing school-wide administrative standards and ensuring alignment with HASS priorities. Establish and maintain standardized procedures, office systems, and confidential records in accordance with Institute policies. Department-Level Event and Program Coordination: Plan and manage recurring departmental events and initiatives, such as colloquia, exhibitions, symposia, and guest lectures, in alignment with HASS strategic goals. Coordinate event logistics and vendor arrangements, partner with the Business Office on budgeting and financial tracking, and work with the Operations Team to publicize and document events across school and Institute channels. Academic Hiring and Search Coordination: Manage the administrative process for faculty and academic staff searches at the department level, in coordination with search committees and the Manager of Administrative Operations. Ensure compliance with Institute and legal requirements, track candidate data, and oversee travel and visit logistics. Facilities and Space Administration: Support school-wide space allocation and facilities management by maintaining departmental space records, participating in the HASS Annual Space Survey, coordinating building inspections, and addressing safety requirements in collaboration with the Manager of Administrative Operations. Calendar and Scheduling Coordination: Oversee the scheduling of key department-level activities, meetings, and recurring events to ensure alignment with school priorities. Maintain master departmental calendars to coordinate with HASS-wide scheduling needs. Procurement and Transaction Processing: Initiate and process department-level purchases, reimbursements, and honorariums in compliance with Institute policies. Complete purchase orders and related transactions using OSCAR, process travel and expense reports in CONCUR, and ensure all documentation is accurate and submitted within required timelines. Academic Administration & Compliance: Coordinate department-level responsibilities related to academic processes, including promotion and tenure, faculty workload reporting, and policy compliance, ensuring deadlines are met and records are accurately maintained. Cross-Departmental Collaboration and Special Projects: Collaborate with other Administrative Coordinators to share resources, provide backup coverage, and maintain operational consistency across HASS departments. Contribute to school-wide projects, initiatives, and time-sensitive priorities as directed by the Manager of Administrative Operations, ensuring work supports the strategic and operational goals of the school. Shift: Business Hours: Monday - Friday Travel: No travel Driving: No Driving Starting Salary/Rate: Expected hiring range: $20.00 -23.00 Pay transparency disclosure: The selected candidate’s salary will be determined based on factors that include the available budget, internal equity, and the final candidate’s qualifications, experience, education and other job-related credentials. This hiring range is provided as Rensselaer’s good faith estimate of the expected hiring range at the time of posting. Application instructions: Follow the on-screen prompts to create a brief online profile. Please be ready to upload your resume and cover letter. If you need assistance with the online application process, please contact careers@rpi.edu. Job Posted Date: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Total Compensation and Benefits Information: Rensselaer’s Total Compensation Program is designed to provide stable pay growth, a comprehensive and affordable benefits package, and a comprehensive and affordable retiree medical and prescription plan. Our goal is to provide you and your family with a comprehensive health and welfare program as an umbrella of financial security and protection during your employment. For more information, please visit Benefits | Human Resources (rpi.edu) . Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is committed to the cultivation of a community that is welcoming, inclusive, and above all values learning. We welcome candidates who bring a variety of perspectives to Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute's work and campus communities. Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation or gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or other characteristic protected by law. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 4de53c61 Last Name (required) 6ded3e52 Email (required) 98e60111 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Assistant Coach, Women's Hockey Troy, NY Athletics The duties and responsibilities of the Assistant Coach for Women’s Ice Hockey are to assist the Head Coach in the management and administration of a Division I Women’s Hockey program. The core responsibilities of the Assistant Coach are to recommend, implement and execute a successful recruiting philosophy and strategy to ensure student-athletes are committed and engaged academically, athletically, and socially. In addition, the Assistant Coach is responsible for preparing student-athletes both on and off the ice with instruction of an academic and personal nature. The Assistant Coach will also serve as coordinator for position-specific players and will assist in the development of all position players. Assistant Coach, Women's Lacrosse Troy, NY ICA Sports The Assistant Coach, Women's Lacrosse provides coaching, recruiting, and administrative support to the Head Coach in all aspects of the Women's Lacrosse program. This position assists with planning and conducting practices and competitions, instructing and mentoring student-athletes, identifying and recruiting qualified prospective student-athletes, supporting academic success, and promoting student-athlete development on and off the field. The Assistant Coach also assists with program operations, fundraising, alumni engagement, team travel, NCAA and conference compliance, and other administrative responsibilities that contribute to the success and competitiveness of the Women's Lacrosse program. Deputy Title IX Coordinator / Equal Opportunity Specialist Hybrid: in-office and remote work. Troy, NY Human Resources Office The Deputy Title IX Coordinator / Equal Opportunity Specialist supports the Institute’s commitment to an equitable, inclusive, and discrimination-free living, learning, and working environment. The position provides dedicated support for the effective administration of the Institute’s Title IX, Equal Opportunity, Title VI, and related civil rights compliance programs, helping ensure fair, thorough, and supportive processes for all participants. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert f2f5d422 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administrative Support Staff Administrative Support Staff Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Troy, NY, New York, United States Troy, NY, New York, United States First Name (required) 40cd7f84 Last Name (required) 721acb36 Email (required) e9047812 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026 Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute (RPI) Cookie Preferences Web Privacy TileX Student Consumer Information Accessibilityy Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
