    "https://careers.rpi.edu/jobs/director-sport-performance-and-wellness-troy-ny-new-york-united-states": {
      "title": "Director, Sport Performance and Wellness",
      "description": "Director, Sport Performance and Wellness - Troy, NY, New York, United States Back to RPI Website My Profile Kiosk mode Director, Sport Performance and Wellness Troy, NY Athletics Business, Accounting and Finance Staff Full Time Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary: The Director, Sport Performance & Wellness is responsible for leading and managing the newly formed area of Sport Performance & Wellness in RPI Athletics. The Director will serve as the strategic oversight of data collection and integration to best enhance the safety and performance of our student-athletes. With direct oversight of the Strength & Conditioning unit, the Director will advise coaches on how to utilize this data for programming and work closely with Athletic Training to ensure training cycles support the wellbeing of student-athletes. This position will design and implement strength and conditioning sessions for our Division I hockey programs. Who we are: Founded in 1824, Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute (RPI) is the first technological research university in the United States. We bring creativity, science, and technology together to address society's greatest challenges. We cultivate exceptional problem-solvers by immersing them in a culture of rigorous inquiry, disciplined practice, and hands-on application. Our strategic plan, RPI Forward, charts a pioneering course for the next era of RPI. Explore the RPI Forward plan. ↗︎ Nestled on a beautiful 275-acre campus in upstate NY, RPI is home to five schools, 32 research centers, three makerspaces, an observatory, one of the world’s fastest supercomputers, and the IBM Quantum System One - the first university-based quantum computer in the world. With top notch employee health and retirement benefits, Rensselaer offers its full-time employees a generous paid time off program, tuition remission, and opportunities for career growth. Minimum Qualifications: 3 or more years as a head coach in the field of strength and conditioning or in a professional sport setting supporting the strength and conditioning development of athletes Working knowledge of the game of ice hockey Strength and Conditioning Specialist Certification and/or NSCA Certification Relevant combinations of education, training and experience may be considered. Minimum Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Experience or certification in sport-related nutrition Knowledge of strength training, speed, agility, flexibility, and cardiovascular conditioning Knowledge of NCAA regulations and guidelines Demonstrated ability to motivate high-performing student-athletes Ability to initiate, develop and maintain contacts appropriate to developing an effective strength and conditioning program Knowledge of sport-related data including Catapult, Velocity-Based Training, and other wearables Ability to convey a clear and concise message while communicating, both verbally and in writing Ability to work effectively with a wide range of constituents Ability to read, design and enforce safety procedures Ability to foster a cooperative work environment Ability to work effectively under pressure and meet established goals and objectives Ability to make administrative/procedural decisions and judgments Representative Job Duties: Manage all aspects of sport-related data and wearable technology used across the athletic department. Ensure coaches, student-athletes, and staff (athletic training/strength and conditioning) are well trained in how to incorporate feedback from the data to design, adjust, and execute high-level training cycles that support student-athlete wellbeing. Present results of the data, as well as student-athlete performance and potential enhancements to programming, annually to the head coaches and director of athletics. Provide supervision, direction, and guidance to strength and conditioning staff, including recommendations related to best practices in athlete performance and recovery. Prepare guidelines for interns or others who are working in the strength and conditioning unit. Educate student-athletes on correct techniques of weightlifting, plyometrics, speed development drills, conditioning exercises, and agility movements. Design monthly sessions that educate strength and conditioning staff on industry trends. Ensure staff seek and complete necessary educational experiences to maintain certification(s). Assist with the coordination of wellness support for our Division I student-athletes in alignment with the NCAA Student-Athlete Core Guarantees, including education related to mental health, strength and conditioning, and nutrition. Collaborate with external partners to provide support in areas such as Sport Psychology or Sport Mental Performance. Work closely with Athletic Training staff to ensure an open line of communication between strength and conditioning staff in terms of rehabilitation and reinstatement of student-athletes in practice and competitions. Serve as a member of the Athletic Department Senior Staff, advising the strategic direction of the athletic department. Act as an advocate for student-athlete wellbeing and serve on campus committees supporting similar efforts. Maintain up-to-date manuals and SOPs for Strength and Conditioning, as well as Data Analytics or Use of Student-Athlete Performance Data. Perform other duties as assigned in support of the athletic department’s overall mission and operations. Shift: Primarily business hours; however, occasional evenings, weekends, and non-traditional hours are required based on student-athlete training needs, competition schedules, and departmental priorities. Travel: Travel is a significant component of the position (greater than 25%) and includes team travel, athletic events, professional development activities, and other department-related commitments. Driving: Incidental driving possible, but not required Starting Salary/Rate: Expected hiring range: $80,000 - $85,000 Pay transparency disclosure: The selected candidate’s salary will be determined based on factors that include the available budget, internal equity, and the final candidate’s qualifications, experience, education and other job-related credentials. This hiring range is provided as Rensselaer’s good faith estimate of the expected hiring range at the time of posting. Application instructions: Follow the on-screen prompts to create a brief online profile. Please be ready to upload your resume and cover letter. If you need assistance with the online application process, please contact careers@rpi.edu. Job Posted Date: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Total Compensation and Benefits Information: Rensselaer’s Total Compensation Program is designed to provide stable pay growth, a comprehensive and affordable benefits package, and a comprehensive and affordable retiree medical and prescription plan. Our goal is to provide you and your family with a comprehensive health and welfare program as an umbrella of financial security and protection during your employment. For more information, please visit Benefits | Human Resources (rpi.edu) . Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is committed to the cultivation of a community that is welcoming, inclusive, and above all values learning. We welcome candidates who bring a variety of perspectives to Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute's work and campus communities. Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation or gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or other characteristic protected by law. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 7192bac7 Last Name (required) 84d9337f Email (required) fc59932d Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Assistant Coach, Women's Hockey Troy, NY Athletics The duties and responsibilities of the Assistant Coach for Women’s Ice Hockey are to assist the Head Coach in the management and administration of a Division I Women’s Hockey program. The core responsibilities of the Assistant Coach are to recommend, implement and execute a successful recruiting philosophy and strategy to ensure student-athletes are committed and engaged academically, athletically, and socially. In addition, the Assistant Coach is responsible for preparing student-athletes both on and off the ice with instruction of an academic and personal nature. The Assistant Coach will also serve as coordinator for position-specific players and will assist in the development of all position players. Assistant Coach, Women's Lacrosse Troy, NY ICA Sports The Assistant Coach, Women's Lacrosse provides coaching, recruiting, and administrative support to the Head Coach in all aspects of the Women's Lacrosse program. This position assists with planning and conducting practices and competitions, instructing and mentoring student-athletes, identifying and recruiting qualified prospective student-athletes, supporting academic success, and promoting student-athlete development on and off the field. The Assistant Coach also assists with program operations, fundraising, alumni engagement, team travel, NCAA and conference compliance, and other administrative responsibilities that contribute to the success and competitiveness of the Women's Lacrosse program. Deputy Title IX Coordinator / Equal Opportunity Specialist Hybrid: in-office and remote work. Troy, NY Human Resources Office The Deputy Title IX Coordinator / Equal Opportunity Specialist supports the Institute’s commitment to an equitable, inclusive, and discrimination-free living, learning, and working environment. The position provides dedicated support for the effective administration of the Institute’s Title IX, Equal Opportunity, Title VI, and related civil rights compliance programs, helping ensure fair, thorough, and supportive processes for all participants. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 3644b03d Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Athletics Business, Accounting and Finance Staff Athletics Business, Accounting and Finance Staff Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Troy, NY, New York, United States Troy, NY, New York, United States First Name (required) aede1b80 Last Name (required) 9bd41bf7 Email (required) 2b59283f Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026 Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute (RPI) Cookie Preferences Web Privacy TileX Student Consumer Information Accessibilityy Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
