    "https://careers.rpi.edu/jobs/computer-operator-troy-ny-new-york-united-states-4908b513-4d59-43b9-9215-f5d4641630cf": {
      "title": "Computer Operator",
      "description": "Computer Operator - Troy, NY, New York, United States Back to RPI Website My Profile Kiosk mode Computer Operator Troy, NY CFHE Information Technology Staff Full Time Add to favorites View favorites Who we are Founded in 1824, Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute (RPI) is the first technological research university in the United States. We bring creativity, science, and technology together to address society's greatest challenges. We cultivate exceptional problem-solvers by immersing them in a culture of rigorous inquiry, disciplined practice, and hands-on application. Our strategic plan, RPI Forward, charts a pioneering course for the next era of RPI. Explore the RPI Forward plan. ↗︎ Nestled on a beautiful 275-acre campus in upstate NY, RPI is home to five schools, 32 research centers, three makerspaces, an observatory, one of the world’s fastest supercomputers, and the IBM Quantum System One - the first university-based quantum computer in the world. With top notch employee health and retirement benefits, Rensselaer offers its full-time employees a generous paid time off program, tuition remission, and opportunities for career growth. Job Summary The Computer Operator performs standard operational procedures and provides support services for internal and external users of the computers and peripheral equipment. The Computer Operator is responsible for the accurate and timely processing of information and services in a multi-disciplined computing environment, including and monitoring application programs and systems utilities, and quality control. Minimum Qualifications High school diploma or GED. At least 1 year of experience working with computer and network equipment and operating software. Valid U.S. driver’s license and reliable transportation. Note: Relevant combinations of education, training, and experience may also be considered. Preferred Qualifications Associate’s degree in IT, Science, Engineering, or a related field. Basic coding or scripting skills in any language or system. Basic mechanical aptitude for assembling and repairing items. Minimum Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of Microsoft products and computer networks. Requires planning, organizing and effective time management skills. Requires excellent interpersonal and communication skills. Requires ability to anticipate and solve problems. Ability to work independently, under pressure in a variety of technical situations and meet established goals and objectives. Requires excellent customer service skills Preferred Knowledge, Skill, and Abilities Any certificates in Networking or Telecommunication Any certificate in System Administration Linux or Microsoft Any certificates in Basic Database utilization/creation Representative Job Duties Monitor the status of computer rooms and perform physical checks to ensure safe and continued operation of equipment such as HVAC. Monitor temperature and humidity levels to prevent adverse environmental impact to major systems. Monitor the operation of services, including computers, printers, networks, and phone systems, identify service irregularities and equipment failures. Execute standard operating procedures or contact support staff when conditions warrant action. Record observations, respond to issues as they occur, and execute standard operating procedures. Contact support staff when conditions warrant action Execute procedures for managing offsite tape handling following standard procedures and maintain security of password lists and key. Patrol remote campus locations and complete security checks, monitor and maintain status of equipment and resolve issues as needed. Provide customer support including, handle and distribute printer and plotter output, install and remove equipment from computer rooms, rebooting servers or executing specific procedures on equipment, respond to phone and e-mail inquiries, assess the nature of reported problems, and execute standard operating procedures. Maintain VCC, CII and remote computer supply areas, receive deliveries, put away supplies, complete necessary paperwork according to policies and procedures and notify supervisor of low supply levels to ensure appropriate levels are available. Update and provide documentation regarding systems and store relevant data according to established procedures into operations database(s). Promote building and lab security by following walk through and lockup procedures. - Participate in processes to improve operational activities. Maintain appropriate practices to ensure confidentially and security of data, especially with the regards to mandated requirements (i.e. FERPA, HIPPA, PCI, etc.) Shift 3rd Shift: 11:00pm - 7:30am; Wednesday, Thursday, Friday, Saturday, Sunday (ending Monday morning at 7:30am) This position is considered an essential role. Travel Local travel between campus locations only Driving Driving a personal vehicle for non-passenger use Starting Salary/Rate Expected hiring range: $18.00 per hour ($0.75 hourly differential) Pay transparency disclosure: The selected candidate’s salary will be determined based on factors that include the available budget, internal equity, and the final candidate’s qualifications, experience, education and other job-related credentials. This hiring range is provided as Rensselaer’s good faith estimate of the expected hiring range at the time of posting. Application instructions Follow the on-screen prompts to create a brief online profile. Please be ready to upload your resume and cover letter. If you need assistance with the online application process, please contact careers@rpi.edu. Job Posted Date Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Total Compensation and Benefits Information Rensselaer’s Total Compensation Program is designed to provide stable pay growth, a comprehensive and affordable benefits package, and a comprehensive and affordable retiree medical and prescription plan. Our goal is to provide you and your family with a comprehensive health and welfare program as an umbrella of financial security and protection during your employment. For more information, please visit Benefits | Human Resources (rpi.edu) . Rensselaer is committed to the cultivation of a community that is welcoming, inclusive, and above all values learning. We welcome candidates who bring a variety of perspectives to Rensselaer’s work and campus communities. RPI is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation or gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or other characteristic protected by law. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 70fd0104 Last Name (required) 6bb014f9 Email (required) 621e33fe Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Assistant Coach, Women's Hockey Troy, NY Athletics The duties and responsibilities of the Assistant Coach for Women’s Ice Hockey are to assist the Head Coach in the management and administration of a Division I Women’s Hockey program. The core responsibilities of the Assistant Coach are to recommend, implement and execute a successful recruiting philosophy and strategy to ensure student-athletes are committed and engaged academically, athletically, and socially. In addition, the Assistant Coach is responsible for preparing student-athletes both on and off the ice with instruction of an academic and personal nature. The Assistant Coach will also serve as coordinator for position-specific players and will assist in the development of all position players. Assistant Coach, Women's Lacrosse Troy, NY ICA Sports The Assistant Coach, Women's Lacrosse provides coaching, recruiting, and administrative support to the Head Coach in all aspects of the Women's Lacrosse program. This position assists with planning and conducting practices and competitions, instructing and mentoring student-athletes, identifying and recruiting qualified prospective student-athletes, supporting academic success, and promoting student-athlete development on and off the field. The Assistant Coach also assists with program operations, fundraising, alumni engagement, team travel, NCAA and conference compliance, and other administrative responsibilities that contribute to the success and competitiveness of the Women's Lacrosse program. Deputy Title IX Coordinator / Equal Opportunity Specialist Hybrid: in-office and remote work. Troy, NY Human Resources Office The Deputy Title IX Coordinator / Equal Opportunity Specialist supports the Institute’s commitment to an equitable, inclusive, and discrimination-free living, learning, and working environment. The position provides dedicated support for the effective administration of the Institute’s Title IX, Equal Opportunity, Title VI, and related civil rights compliance programs, helping ensure fair, thorough, and supportive processes for all participants. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 8c50d09d Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories CFHE Information Technology Staff CFHE Information Technology Staff Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Troy, NY, New York, United States Troy, NY, New York, United States First Name (required) 4549c1ae Last Name (required) 5178e4ab Email (required) 1d4b373d Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026 Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute (RPI) Cookie Preferences Web Privacy TileX Student Consumer Information Accessibilityy Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\"