    "https://careers.rpi.edu/jobs/laboratory-supervisor-troy-ny-new-york-united-states": {
      "title": "Laboratory Supervisor",
      "description": "Laboratory Supervisor - Troy, NY, New York, United States Back to RPI Website My Profile Kiosk mode Laboratory Supervisor Troy, NY CFHE Student Services and Academic Support Trades, Service, and Maintenance Full Time Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary: The Laboratory Supervisor is responsible for the instructional laboratories in the department of Civil Engineering including facilities and day to day operations as well as the operation, maintenance and repair of laboratory equipment. The position provides instruction on use of equipment to students, faculty and staff as well as works closely with faculty to provide technical, academic and administrative support for instructional laboratory courses. In addition, the Laboratory Supervisor will provide technical expertise to the Department of Civil of Engineering and the School of Engineering. Who we are: Founded in 1824, Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute (RPI) is the first technological research university in the United States. We bring creativity, science, and technology together to address society's greatest challenges. We cultivate exceptional problem-solvers by immersing them in a culture of rigorous inquiry, disciplined practice, and hands-on application. Our strategic plan, RPI Forward, charts a pioneering course for the next era of RPI. Explore the RPI Forward plan. ↗︎ Nestled on a beautiful 275-acre campus in upstate NY, RPI is home to five schools, 32 research centers, three makerspaces, an observatory, one of the world’s fastest supercomputers, and the IBM Quantum System One - the first university-based quantum computer in the world. With top notch employee health and retirement benefits, Rensselaer offers its full-time employees a generous paid time off program, tuition remission, and opportunities for career growth. Minimum Qualifications: Associate's Degree in Engineering, Engineering Technology, or a related field. A minimum of three (3) years of experience in mechanical testing. Applicants must meet stated minimum education and experience requirements. Minimum Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Proficiency with computer systems and a variety of software applications. Working knowledge of electronic data acquisition systems and servo-hydraulic control systems. Ability to collect, record, and maintain data using appropriate systems, equipment, and techniques. Working knowledge of general machine shop equipment, including drill presses, lathes, milling machines, band saws, and various hand and power tools. Ability to read and interpret technical drawings and specifications. Ability to design, set up, and execute sound experimental procedures. Strong planning, organizational, and time management skills. Ability to maintain accurate, detailed, and organized records. Demonstrated analytical, reasoning, and problem-solving abilities. Ability to work effectively under pressure and meet established deadlines. Ability to remain calm and professional when addressing challenging situations or interactions. Excellent interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively within a team environment. Demonstrated commitment to fostering an inclusive environment and working effectively with individuals from diverse backgrounds. Representative Job Duties: Oversee the day-to-day operation of instructional laboratories in compliance with accreditation standards, safety regulations, and other applicable requirements. Maintain the security of laboratories and equipment and provide access to Teaching Assistants (TAs) and other authorized personnel. Train TAs, faculty, staff, and students on the safe use of laboratory equipment and facilities. Develop and maintain standard operating procedures. Ensure equipment, software, and accessories are operational and performing to established standards. Install, maintain, and repair equipment and accessories; maintain adequate inventory levels; coordinate with vendors and suppliers; and provide input on equipment purchases and upgrades. Provide technical assistance to faculty, TAs, and students during instructional activities. Troubleshoot and repair equipment, advise students on laboratory procedures, and serve as a technical resource for the department and School of Engineering. Assist faculty in the development of instructional materials and experiments by providing technical expertise and feedback. Train TAs to facilitate laboratory experiments. Research, identify, and recommend new equipment and upgrades. Coordinate with vendors to arrange demonstrations, deliveries, and installations. Manage instructional laboratory facilities and physical spaces, including coordinating maintenance and repairs and serving as the technical lead for renovations and relocations. Serve as the Laboratory Safety Officer and partner with Environmental Health and Safety to maintain a safe working environment. Actively participate on the School of Engineering Safety Committee. Support School of Engineering outreach initiatives through participation in open houses, STEM presentations, and laboratory tours for internal and external audiences. Perform other duties as assigned. Shift: Business Hours: Monday - Friday Starting Salary/Rate: Expected hiring range: $62,354- $65,000 Pay transparency disclosure: The selected candidate’s salary will be determined based on factors that include the available budget, internal equity, and the final candidate’s qualifications, experience, education and other job-related credentials. This hiring range is provided as Rensselaer’s good faith estimate of the expected hiring range at the time of posting. Application instructions: Follow the on-screen prompts to create a brief online profile. Please be ready to upload your resume and cover letter. If you need assistance with the online application process, please contact careers@rpi.edu. Job Posted Date: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Total Compensation and Benefits Information: Rensselaer’s Total Compensation Program is designed to provide stable pay growth, a comprehensive and affordable benefits package, and a comprehensive and affordable retiree medical and prescription plan. Our goal is to provide you and your family with a comprehensive health and welfare program as an umbrella of financial security and protection during your employment. For more information, please visit Benefits | Human Resources (rpi.edu) . Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is committed to the cultivation of a community that is welcoming, inclusive, and above all values learning. We welcome candidates who bring a variety of perspectives to Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute's work and campus communities. Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation or gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or other characteristic protected by law. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 41d074c2 Last Name (required) a628261a Email (required) 093a20cd Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Assistant Coach, Women's Hockey Troy, NY Athletics The duties and responsibilities of the Assistant Coach for Women’s Ice Hockey are to assist the Head Coach in the management and administration of a Division I Women’s Hockey program. The core responsibilities of the Assistant Coach are to recommend, implement and execute a successful recruiting philosophy and strategy to ensure student-athletes are committed and engaged academically, athletically, and socially. In addition, the Assistant Coach is responsible for preparing student-athletes both on and off the ice with instruction of an academic and personal nature. The Assistant Coach will also serve as coordinator for position-specific players and will assist in