esources Center (1 items) Student Transitions (1 items) Undergraduate Enrollment Programs (2 items) Work Type Search employment types 3 filter options found Work Type Full Time (45 items) Part Time (8 items) Seasonal or Temporary (9 items) Locations Search cities 3 filter options found Locations Hybrid: in-office and remote work (5 items) Remote (US Only) (1 items) Troy, NY (47 items) Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Groundskeeper or Groundskeeper, Sr. Troy, NY Environmental & Site Services Staff Trades, Service, and Maintenance Full Time The Groundskeeper performs grounds and landscape duties, snow removal and equipment operations associated with the maintenance of the campus grounds and athletic fields and support all campus wide events. Read more Counselor I (10-months) Troy, NY Student Support & Resources Center CFHE Health Services Staff Full Time The Counselor I will facilitate the normal developmental process of Rensselaer students, and assist students whose normal developmental process is being impeded by adjustment problems and other disorders. This role will work with students individually and in groups, as well as proactively work with the Rensselaer Community to create an environment that will allow students to maximize their personal growth. The Counselor will also develop and implement mental health prevention and education programs. (NOTE: This is a 10-month role with a scheduled work period of August 1 through May 31 of the following year. The position will enter the non-work period beginning June 1, extending through July 31. This role is eligible for year-round benefits and ability to spread salary over 12-months.) Read more Library Associate (10-months) Troy, NY Library Information Services CFHE Information Technology Staff Student Services and Academic Support Show More Show Less Full Time The Library Associate is primarily responsible for providing customer service at the Libraries’ Service Desks and using information systems for circulation, class reserves and Interlibrary Loan. This position may also coordinate daily collection management, provide training to student workers, and assist with materials and transactional processing.\n\nNOTE: This is a 10-month role with a scheduled work period of August 1 through May 31 of the following year. The position will enter the non-work period beginning June 1, extending through July 31. This role is eligible for year-round benefits. Read more Repairer, Rensselaer Tech Park Troy, NY Rensselaer Technology Park Staff Trades, Service, and Maintenance Full Time The Repairer performs basic repair and maintenance assignments on facilities and equipment using a variety of trades such as, but not limited to, carpentry, mechanical, electrical, plumbing, painting, and masonry. The Repairer also works as a part of a team to complete larger scale renovations. The Repairer participates in on-call rotation for off-hour repairs in Technology Park offices, Pat’s Barn and tenant leased facilities. Read more Associate Director, Career Development Troy, NY Student Transitions CFHE Staff Student Affairs Professionals Student Services and Academic Support Show More Show Less Full Time The Associate Director, Career Development provides strategic leadership and operational oversight for the career development functions of the Center for Career and Professional Development. Reporting to the Assistant Vice Provost for Experiential Learning and Professional Development, this position leads a comprehensive portfolio of career education services designed to prepare students and alumni for successful career outcomes, including career coaching, career education programming, career readiness initiatives, and career-related resources. Read more Assistant Strength & Conditioning Coach Troy, NY Dean of Students CFHE Staff Student Services and Academic Support Full Time The Assistant Strength & Conditioning Coach will serve as a fitness content expert and provide management and programming for an innovative, dynamic, and collaborative effort to promote a culture of integrated well-being. This position will be responsible for continuing the growth, implementation, and evaluation of comprehensive movement and exercise programs. This position will serve as the primary strength and conditioning coach for 58 club sports and work closely with colleagues to market and evaluate movement experiences and programs. This position provides direct supervision to a team of student employees. The Assistant Strength & Conditioning Coach reports to the Director of Mueller Center, RecWell and Club Sports. Read more Project Administrator Troy, NY Ctr for Mats, Devs & Int Sys Administrative Support CFHE Research: Microelectronics Researchers and Research Support Staff Show More Show Less Full Time Support innovative semiconductor research initiatives while coordinating projects, events, and daily operations for RPI's Semiconductor CoLaboratory and UPWARDS program. Join a collaborative team advancing workforce development and cutting-edge research in microelectronics. Read more Lecturer, Electrical, Computer and Systems Engineering (ECSE) Troy, NY Electrical, Computer, & Systems Eng CFHE School of Engineering Full Time The Department of Electrical, Computer and Systems Engineering (ECSE) at Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute invites applications for a full-time Lecturer. Candidates from all ECSE disciplines are encouraged to apply, with particular interest in electronics (including analog and mixed-signal integrated circuit design), computer architecture, control and robotics, and artificial intelligence. The successful candidate will contribute to the department's teaching mission through instruction in undergraduate and graduate courses and support of the core engineering curriculum. A Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, or a closely related field is required. Read more Mover & Grounds Specialist Troy, NY Environmental & Site Services Staff Trades, Service, and Maintenance Full Time The Mover & Grounds Specialist at Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute supports campus operations by performing moves, event setup and breakdown, snow removal, and grounds maintenance using various equipment. This hands-on role requires strong customer service, equipment operation skills, and the flexibility to work varied hours to help maintain the safety and appearance of the university’s 275-acre campus. Read more Associate Director, International Recruitment & Global Partnerships Hybrid: in-office and remote work Troy, NY Undergraduate Enrollment Programs CFHE Staff Student Services and Academic Support Full Time The Associate Director of International Enrollment provides strategic leadership for RPI’s global recruitment efforts, overseeing international admissions strategy, recruitment staff, agent partnerships, and compliance with federal immigration regulations. This role leads multi-week international recruitment travel across priority markets, drives data-informed enrollment and yield strategies, and partners across campus to support financial aid, pathway programs, and international student success. The position requires extensive global travel and active engagement during peak recruitment and yield seasons. Read more Cleaner - Environmental Specialist Troy, NY Environmental & Site Services Staff Trades, Service, and Maintenance Full Time The Department of Environmental Services seeks applicants to fill its opening for several Cleaner openings. Read more Public Safety Officer I Troy, NY Public Safety Office Public Safety Full Time Entry level Public Safety opportunities available for service minded individuals interested in facilitating a safe and secure environment for the students, faculty, and staff who live, learn and work at Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute. Read more Aerospace Engineering Faculty (Lecturer, Senior Lecturer, or Professor of Practice) Troy, NY Mech, Aero & Nuclear Engineering CFHE Faculty School of Engineering Full Time The Department of Mechanical, Aerospace, and Nuclear Engineering (MANE) at Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute (RPI) invites applications for a full-time Lecturer, Senior Lecturer, or Professor of Practice in Aerospace Engineering. The successful candidate will contribute to the department's teaching mission by delivering high-quality instruction, mentoring students, and participating in departmental, institute, and professional service activities. Areas of interest include, but are not limited to, space vehicle design, space navigation, space structures and control, space environments, and human factors. Candidates with expertise in other aerospace engineering disciplines are also encouraged to apply. This position offers an opportunity to join a growing and collaborative department with a strong legacy in aerospace innovation and space exploration. Read more Proposal Administrator, Sr.  ( Hybrid or Remote ) Remote (US Only) Hybrid: in-office and remote work Troy, NY Research and Financial Administratn Business, Accounting and Finance CFHE Full Time Join Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute as a Sr. Proposal Administrator and play a key role in supporting cutting-edge research initiatives through expert proposal review, compliance, and submission management. This highly collaborative position partners with faculty and campus stakeholders to navigate complex federal, state, foundation, and industry-sponsored funding opportunities. Ideal candidates bring strong pre-award research administration experience, deep knowledge of federal regulations, and a passion for supporting innovation in a fast-paced higher education environment. Read more EMPAC Overhire Pool Troy, NY EMPAC General EMPAC Staff Part Time Seasonal or Temporary Part time and/or occasional staff needed to assist the Experimental Media & Performing Arts Center (EMPAC) team in preparing for events and management of attendees. Read more Sr. Research Scientist Troy, NY CFES Ctr for Future Energy Systems CFHE Research: Materials & Manufacturing Research: Microelectronics Researchers and Research Support Show More Show Less Full Time The Sr. Research Scientist leads advanced research at the Center, overseeing the Power Electronics Applications Laboratory (PEAL) and driving collaborations with the power electronics industry. This role manages PEAL operations, lab safety, and supervision of users, while supporting industrial partners in testing, characterization, and modeling of power electronics, including wide bandgap devices and power converters. The Scientist also helps develop research partnerships and innovative solutions leveraging PEAL capabilities. Read more Field House Temp Staff Troy, NY Field House Athletics Staff Part Time Seasonal or Temporary Incumbents are hired on an if/when needed basis during events at the Houston Field House. Representative assignments include: \nParking Lot Attendant, Usher, Zamboni Driver, Box Office Clerk, Ticket Taker, and Sound Technician. Read more Displaying 31 - 47 of 47 in total ‹ 1 2 › Powered by PageUp Sign up for job alerts Job Alert e48fb4c5 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Employment Type Locations First Name (required) aaa35c2a Last Name (required) cbeddba1 Email (required) 78c5a66e Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026 Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute (RPI) Cookie Preferences Web Privacy TileX Student Consumer Information Accessibilityy Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the opera